(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('significantly','Significant comes through French from Latin significant- (stem of significans, “indicating”); -ly forms the adverb. The adverb can mark either an important degree or a statistically meaningful result.',C('significantly.s1','research','After the second trial, the treatment group scored significantly higher than the control group.','第二轮试验后，治疗组的得分显著高于对照组。','scored significantly higher','significantly 修饰比较级 higher，说明差距达到有意义的程度。','In a research report, significantly may describe a statistically meaningful difference, not merely a large-looking one.','研究结果中该词还可指具有统计意义。'),M('The treatment group scored significantly higher, but the measured difference was only a rounding artifact and the report calls it meaningful.','The treatment group scored significantly higher, with a difference large enough to be statistically meaningful.','显著性不能由舍入误差冒充；此处必须有可检验的实质差异。','context'),[Q(1,'What does significantly higher mean in the trial report?','higher by a meaningful, tested amount','higher only because the chart uses a larger font','exactly equal to the control score','The adverb signals a meaningful difference, often statistical in research.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses significantly most precisely?','The intervention significantly reduced errors in the tested sample.','The page was significantly printed in blue ink.','The unchanged scores significantly matched exactly.','It modifies a measured result whose change matters.'),Q(1,'In a data report, significantly can indicate a result is…','statistically meaningful under the test used','guaranteed to matter to every patient','a synonym for slightly, with no evidence','The word is also used for statistical significance.'),Q(1,'Which is a natural placement for this adverb?','The rate fell significantly after the filter was installed.','The rate significantly the filter after installation.','The significantly was rate falling filter.','Significantly modifies the verb phrase fell.')]);
P('signification','Signification entered English through French from Latin significatio, “indication, meaning,” from significare, “to signify.”',C('signification.s1','linguistics','The signification of the red ribbon changes from one ceremony to another.','红丝带所代表的意义会随仪式不同而变化。','signification of the red ribbon','of 短语限定符号所表达的意思。','The noun names the meaning carried by a sign or expression.','它指符号或表达所承载的意义。'),M('In this poem, the signification of the dove is the bird’s wingspan measured in centimetres.','In this poem, the signification of the dove is the peace it represents.','signification 是象征或表达的意义，不是物体的物理尺寸。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What is the signification of the ribbon in the example?','what it represents in each ceremony','how many centimetres long it is','the date printed on the box','Signification is the meaning represented by a sign.'),Q(1,'Which item has a signification in a written code?','a red mark that stands for “approved”','the paper’s weight alone','the pen’s purchase price','A mark may carry a meaning within a code.'),Q(1,'Signification is closest to…','meaning conveyed','physical measurement','sound volume','The noun refers to what a symbol or word means.'),Q(1,'Which question asks about signification?','What does this gesture communicate?','How heavy is the ribbon?','Who made the table?','Signification concerns meaning, not physical properties.')]);
P('signify','Signify comes from Old French signifier and Latin significare, “make a sign, indicate,” from signum “mark, sign.”',[C('signify.s1','symbols','On the map, a blue line signifies a river.','在地图上，蓝线表示河流。','blue line signifies a river','主语 + signify + 宾语，表示符号所指。','Here the mark represents a feature on a map.', '此处 signify 表示某标记代表地图中的地貌。'),C('signify.s2','importance','The delay does not signify that the project has been cancelled.','这次延误并不意味着项目已经取消。','does not signify that','否定结构中 signify 表示“意味着”；宾语为 that 从句。','In negative statements, signify can mean “matter” or “have importance.”','否定句中 signify 也可表示“要紧、有重要性”。')],M('A blue line signifies a river, so the map key says the line represents a desert.','A blue line signifies a river, as the map key explains.','地图标记的含义需与图例一致，不能把河流线解释为沙漠。','context'),[Q(1,'What does the blue line signify?','a river','a mountain range','a railway station','The first sense is to represent or indicate something.'),Q(2,'What does the delay signify in the second example?','It does not mean the project is cancelled.','The project has definitely ended.','The delay is a map symbol for water.','The negative construction denies that the delay means cancellation.'),Q(1,'Which object can signify danger?','a warning light','an unmarked blank page','a number with no agreed code','A sign can indicate a condition such as danger.'),Q(2,'In “It does not signify,” the speaker means “It does not…”','matter or have importance','show the way with a road sign','make a sound louder','The second sense is importance, often in negative phrases.')]);
P('signpost','Signpost is a compound of sign + post: a sign fixed to a post; the verb later extends this idea to marking a route or guiding a reader.',[C('signpost.s1','travel','At the fork, a wooden signpost showed the walking distance to each village.','岔路口的木路标标出了到各村的步行距离。','wooden signpost','名词作主语，后接 showed 引出牌面信息。','A signpost is a physical direction board beside a route.','此处是路边指示方向的牌子。'),C('signpost.s3','writing','The lecturer signposted the shift from evidence to her conclusion with a slide titled “What the results mean.”','讲师用一张题为“结果意味着什么”的幻灯片，清楚提示了从证据转向结论的部分。','signposted the shift','signpost 作及物动词，宾语为读者需要追踪的论证转折。','The verb can make a stage or transition explicit for an audience.','动词义是让听众或读者清楚看到进程节点。')],M('The lecturer signposted the conclusion by removing every heading and giving no clue where the argument changed.','The lecturer signposted the conclusion with a clear heading marking the change in argument.','不提供标题或提示不能称为 signposting；该动词义是明确标示结构。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the wooden signpost provide?','directions and distances to villages','a summary of the lecture','a legal signature','A physical signpost guides travellers.'),Q(3,'How did the lecturer signpost the shift?','by making the transition clear to the audience','by hiding every heading','by changing the road surface','The verb sense means mark a route or structure clearly.'),Q(1,'Which object is a signpost in the literal sense?','a board at a trail junction pointing to towns','a private note kept in a drawer','a map scale printed without directions','The literal compound names a direction sign on a post.'),Q(3,'In an essay, a sentence that previews the next section can…','signpost the argument for readers','silence every reader','measure the paper’s weight','The figurative verb helps readers follow the structure.')]);
P('silence','Silence comes from Old French silence and Latin silentium, from silere “to be quiet”; the noun names quiet or not speaking, and the verb makes something quiet.',[C('silence.s1','conversation','After the accusation, a tense silence settled over the dinner table.','指责之后，餐桌上陷入紧张的沉默。','a tense silence','抽象名词作主语；情绪形容词 tense 描写谈话中断。','The people could have spoken but did not.', '此处是人不发言的沉默。'),C('silence.s2','sound','At dawn, the silence of the snow-covered valley was broken by one bell.','黎明时，积雪山谷的寂静被一声钟响打破。','silence of the valley','of 短语说明没有声音的环境。','The second noun sense is absence of sound, not merely a pause in conversation.','第二义指环境无声。'),C('silence.s3','noise control','The librarian raised one hand to silence the visitors before the reading began.','朗读开始前，图书管理员举起一只手让访客们安静下来。','silence the visitors','silence 作及物动词，宾语是被制止发声的人。','The verb means cause someone or something to become quiet.','动词义是使人或物安静下来。')],M('The librarian silenced the noisy visitors by asking them to shout over the reading.','The librarian silenced the noisy visitors by asking them to lower their voices.','silence 作动词是让声音停止或降低，不是鼓励他们更大声。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What happened after the accusation?','the diners stopped speaking','the room became louder with music','the table disappeared','The first sense is people not speaking.'),Q(2,'What broke the valley’s silence?','one bell','a long conversation at the table','a librarian’s raised hand','Here silence means the absence of sound.'),Q(3,'What did the librarian do?','made the visitors quiet','sent the visitors to another city','asked them to ring the bell','The verb sense means cause people to stop making noise.'),Q(1,'Which phrase describes silence in conversation?','a tense pause when no one answers','a valley with no audible sound','a hand raised to quiet a crowd','This item tests the noun sense of not speaking.')]);
P('silencer','Silencer is formed from silence + -er, naming a device that reduces sound; by extension, it can name a person or thing that stops others speaking.',[C('silencer.s1','engineering','The mechanic replaced a cracked exhaust silencer, and the engine became much quieter.','技工更换了裂开的排气消音器，发动机因此安静了许多。','exhaust silencer','名词修饰名词 exhaust，指降低发动机噪声的部件。','The device dampens noise from an engine.','该装置降低发动机噪声。'),C('silencer.s2','figurative','The sudden legal threat acted as a silencer on witnesses who had been ready to speak.','突然的法律威胁让原本准备作证的人噤了声。','acted as a silencer on witnesses','act as ... on 表示起到压制发言的作用。','Figuratively, a silencer is a person or force that makes others stop talking.','比喻义是让他人闭口的人或力量。')],M('The mechanic fitted an exhaust silencer to make the engine louder and more distracting.','The mechanic fitted an exhaust silencer to reduce the engine noise.','消音器的作用是降低而非放大噪声。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the exhaust silencer change?','it reduced engine noise','it increased the engine’s volume','it measured fuel level','A silencer is a device that cuts sound.'),Q(2,'Why did the witnesses stop speaking?','a legal threat discouraged them','the car exhaust became quieter','they were asked to tune the engine','The figurative sense suppresses people’s speech.'),Q(1,'Which component is a silencer?','a part that reduces exhaust noise','a loudspeaker that amplifies music','a fuel gauge','The device sense concerns sound reduction.'),Q(2,'Calling a threat a silencer suggests it…','stops people from speaking freely','repairs an engine','records testimony','The figurative noun describes a force that makes people quiet.')]);
P('silent','Silent comes through Old French from Latin silent-, the present participle stem of silere “be quiet”; it describes no sound, no speech, or an unpronounced letter.',[C('silent.s1','sound','The studio fell silent as the last note faded.','最后一个音符消散时，录音室安静了下来。','fell silent','fall + adjective 表示进入无声状态。','The adjective describes an absence of sound.','此处表示没有声音。'),C('silent.s2','conversation','Mara stayed silent about the surprise until the guests arrived.','客人到来前，玛拉一直没有透露惊喜的事。','stayed silent about','silent about + topic 表示不谈某事。','This sense is a person choosing not to speak about a topic.','此处指对某话题保持沉默。'),C('silent.s3','pronunciation','The b in “lamb” is silent, although it remains in the spelling.','“lamb”里的 b 不发音，虽然拼写中保留着它。','b in “lamb” is silent','表语 adjective 描写字母不发音。','A silent letter is written but not pronounced.')],M('The final b in “lamb” is silent, so pronounce it clearly as /b/.','The final b in “lamb” is silent, so do not pronounce it.','若字母是 silent，就不应发出该辅音。','usage'),[Q(3,'Which letter is silent in “lamb”?','b','l','a','The final b is written but not pronounced.'),Q(2,'If Mara stayed silent about the surprise, she…','did not talk about it','announced it to every guest','made the room physically soundproof','Silent about a topic means not speaking about it.'),Q(1,'What happened to the studio after the last note?','it became quiet','it began to echo more loudly','it was moved outdoors','Silent can describe a place with no sound.'),Q(3,'A silent letter is…','written but not spoken','spoken but never written','a letter sent without a stamp','The pronunciation sense contrasts spelling with speech.')]);
P('silhouette','Silhouette was borrowed from French silhouette, named after Étienne de Silhouette, whose name became associated with inexpensive profile portraits; it later widened to any dark outline against light.',[C('silhouette.s1','photography','At sunset, the lighthouse appeared as a black silhouette against the orange sky.','日落时，灯塔在橙色天空的衬托下呈现为黑色剪影。','black silhouette against','against 引出明亮背景，突出深色外形。','The first sense is a dark shape seen against a lighter background.','第一义是在亮背景前看到的深色形状。'),C('silhouette.s2','portrait','The artist captured the sitter’s profile silhouette in a single curved line.','画家用一条弧线勾出了模特的侧面轮廓。','profile silhouette','profile 限定从侧面看到的脸部或身形外轮廓。','The second sense refers specifically to an outline viewed from the side.','第二义特指侧面轮廓。')],M('The lighthouse silhouette was a brightly lit, fully detailed front view with no visible outline.','The lighthouse silhouette was a dark outline against the bright sky.','剪影依靠与背景的明暗对比呈现外形，不是细节完备的正面照。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why was the lighthouse a silhouette?','its dark shape stood out against the bright sky','every brick was brightly lit in detail','the sky and tower had identical colors','A silhouette is a dark shape against a lighter background.'),Q(2,'What did the artist capture from the sitter?','the outline of the face seen from the side','the full color of the back of the coat','a written list of the sitter’s words','The side-view outline is the profile sense.'),Q(1,'Which scene shows a silhouette?','a dark tree shape against a pale moon','a detailed bright tree on a dark canvas','a tree measured with a ruler','Contrast with a lighter background makes the shape visible.'),Q(2,'A profile silhouette mainly records…','the side outline of a face or figure','a person’s exact voice','the color of a room’s walls','The second sense is a side-view outline.')]);
P('silica','Silica takes its name from Latin silex, silicis “flint”; chemically it is silicon dioxide, the material found abundantly in quartz and sand.',C('silica.s1','chemistry','The glassmaker heated silica with soda and lime to make the bottle walls.','玻璃工把二氧化硅与纯碱和石灰加热，制成瓶壁。','heated silica with','silica 作化学物质名词，作 heated 的宾语。','Silica is silicon dioxide, a principal ingredient in many kinds of sand and quartz.','硅石即二氧化硅，是沙和石英的主要成分。'),M('The lab report identifies silica as silicon dioxide, SiO₂, but says it contains no silicon or oxygen.','The lab report identifies silica as silicon dioxide, SiO₂, containing silicon and oxygen.','SiO₂ 由硅和氧组成；否认其中有这两种元素自相矛盾。','context'),[Q(1,'What is silica chemically?','silicon dioxide, SiO₂','pure metallic silver','sodium chloride only','Silica is silicon dioxide.'),Q(1,'Why was silica added in the glassmaking example?','it is a main glass-forming material','it is a kind of fabric','it measures the bottle’s volume','The source sense names SiO₂, used in glass.'),Q(1,'Which material commonly contains much silica?','quartz','silk thread','wood ash alone','Quartz is largely crystalline silica.'),Q(1,'Which formula represents silica?','SiO₂','H₂O','NaCl','Silica consists of silicon and oxygen in a 1:2 ratio.')]);
P('silicate','Silicate combines silica with the chemical suffix -ate, used for a salt or anion; silicate minerals contain silicon and oxygen with metal elements.',C('silicate.s1','geology','Feldspar is a silicate mineral containing silicon, oxygen, and metals such as potassium or calcium.','长石是一种含硅、氧及钾或钙等金属元素的硅酸盐矿物。','silicate mineral','名词短语点明这类矿物的化学组成。','A silicate is a salt or mineral built around silicon–oxygen units combined with metals.','此处是硅氧与金属结合而成的盐类矿物。'),M('The geologist classified feldspar as a silicate even though the sample contained only carbon and hydrogen.','The geologist classified feldspar as a silicate because it contains silicon and oxygen with metals.','硅酸盐需有硅氧结构；只有碳氢的样品不符合该组成。','context'),[Q(1,'Which composition fits a silicate mineral?','silicon and oxygen combined with metal elements','only carbon and hydrogen','silver mixed with silk fibers','Silicate minerals contain silicon–oxygen units and often metals.'),Q(1,'Why is feldspar described as a silicate?','its mineral structure includes silicon and oxygen','it is a soft fabric','it is made from a single metal only','Silicate identifies a chemical mineral family.'),Q(1,'A silicate belongs to which field?','mineral chemistry','textile sewing','music performance','The word names a chemical/mineral class.'),Q(1,'Which material is most plausibly a silicate?','a quartz-rich mineral with metal ions','a pure cotton thread','a wooden window sill','Silicate compounds are common minerals in rocks.')]);
P('siliceous','Siliceous is formed from silica (with the Latin-derived adjectival ending -eous) and means made of or rich in silica.',C('siliceous.s1','geology','The siliceous sandstone scratched the glass because it contained abundant quartz grains.','这块富含二氧化硅的砂岩划伤了玻璃，因为其中石英颗粒很多。','siliceous sandstone','形容词修饰岩石，说明其富含 silica。','The adjective describes rock or material made of or rich in silica.','该形容词表示由硅石构成或富含硅石。'),M('The sample is called siliceous because chemical analysis found abundant silica in it, yet the note defines siliceous as containing none.','The sample is called siliceous because chemical analysis found abundant silica in it.','siliceous 正表示含硅石，不能同时定义为完全不含 silica。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the sandstone scratch glass?','it contained abundant quartz grains','it was made of soft silk','it contained no minerals','Quartz-rich siliceous rock can be hard enough to scratch glass.'),Q(1,'A siliceous sample is…','made of or rich in silica','made only of silver','free of silicon dioxide','Siliceous means containing much silica.'),Q(1,'Which description fits siliceous rock?','rich in silicon dioxide','woven from silkworm thread','without any mineral content','The adjective refers to silica content.'),Q(1,'How is siliceous related to silica?','it is the adjective meaning containing or made of silica','it is a verb meaning to melt glass','it is a unit of distance','The suffix forms an adjective from silica.')]);
P('silicon','Silicon was coined in 1817 by Jöns Jacob Berzelius from silica with the chemical-element ending -on; it is the element Si, distinct from silicone.',C('silicon.s1','technology','The solar panel converts light to electricity using a thin layer of crystalline silicon.','太阳能板利用一层薄薄的晶体硅把光转化为电能。','crystalline silicon','形容词修饰元素名，指出芯片和太阳能材料常见形态。','Silicon is the chemical element Si used in semiconductor devices and glassmaking.','silicon 是硅元素，可用于半导体器件和玻璃制造。'),M('The technician replaced the silicon chip with silicone sealant because the two names identify the same material and function.','The technician replaced the silicon chip with another silicon component; silicone sealant is a different material.','silicon 是元素硅，silicone 是含硅聚合物，两者不能当作同一种器件材料。','confusable'),[Q(1,'What role does silicon play in the panel?','it forms a light-converting semiconductor layer','it is the panel’s glass coating only','it stores sunlight as a liquid fuel','Silicon is a common semiconductor used in solar cells.'),Q(1,'Which symbol is the element silicon?','Si','S','Sn','The chemical symbol for silicon is Si.'),Q(1,'Silicon should not be confused with silicone, which is…','a distinct silicon-containing polymer material','another name for the element symbol Si','a kind of silver coin','The element and the polymer are distinct substances.'),Q(1,'Why was silicon named with the ending -on?','Berzelius coined it as a chemical-element name from silica','it is a French word for silk clothing','it means a device that silences sound','The modern element name was coined from silica with -on.')]);
P('silk','Silk came into English through Old English sioloc and Latin sericum, ultimately from Greek Serikos “of the Seres”; the ancient name referred to silk associated with China.',[C('silk.s1','textiles','The lining is pure silk, woven from the fine thread produced by silkworms.','这件内衬是纯丝绸，由蚕吐出的细丝织成。','pure silk','材料名词作表语，指蚕丝或其织物。','Silk can mean the natural filament or the smooth cloth woven from it.','silk 可指天然丝线或由其织成的布料。'),C('silk.s2','description','A silk ribbon slid smoothly through the narrow loop.','一条丝质缎带顺滑地穿过窄环。','silk ribbon','名词作定语，表示丝制的；也可作形容词。','The source also uses silk adjectivally for something made of silk or smooth like it.','该词也能作形容词，表示丝制或丝般光滑。')],M('The scarf is silk because it is woven from rough steel wire and feels abrasive.','The scarf is silk because it is woven from fine, smooth silkworm fibre.','丝绸以柔软光滑见称；粗糙钢丝不是丝纤维。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What is the lining made from?','fine thread produced by silkworms','metal wire','tree bark','Silk is the thread or cloth produced from silkworm fibre.'),Q(2,'What does silk describe in “a silk ribbon”?','a ribbon made of silk','a ribbon that makes no sound','a ribbon used to measure a sill','Silk can function adjectivally for material.'),Q(1,'Which statement about silk is accurate?','it can name both fibre and woven cloth','it is the chemical symbol for silicon','it is a type of river sediment','The noun covers the natural filament and the textile.'),Q(1,'The ancient name Serikos was associated with…','the Seres and silk from China','a Greek word for silence','a Roman measurement of six','The word travelled through Greek and Latin names for silk.')]);
P('silken','Silken is silk + the adjective-forming suffix -en, meaning made partly or wholly of silk; it also describes a smooth, soft quality.',[C('silken.s1','clothing','She tied a silken scarf around the parcel before handing it to the guest.','她把一条丝绸围巾系在包裹上，然后递给客人。','silken scarf','silken 修饰 scarf，描述材料。','In the material sense, silken means made of or partly of silk.','材料义表示用丝绸或部分用丝绸制成。'),C('silken.s2','texture','The singer’s silken voice stayed clear even in the high notes.','歌手柔和悦耳的嗓音即使唱到高音也仍然清晰。','silken voice','比喻性形容词修饰 voice，强调悦耳柔和。','The figurative sense describes a smooth, soft texture or pleasant sound.','引申义描述柔滑质地或悦耳声音。')],M('Her silken voice was harsh, scratchy, and unpleasant to listen to throughout the song.','Her silken voice was smooth and pleasant to listen to throughout the song.','silken 的比喻义指柔和悦耳，与刺耳难听相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What was the scarf made of?','silk or partly silk fabric','silica powder','river mud','Silken in this use refers to material.'),Q(2,'What quality did the singer’s silken voice have?','a smooth, pleasant sound','a scratchy, grating sound','a measured length of six inches','The figurative sense describes a soft, pleasing sound.'),Q(1,'Which item is literally silken?','a scarf woven from silk','a stone rich in silica','a metal window frame','The material sense is made of silk.'),Q(2,'A silken texture is most likely…','smooth and soft','coarse and jagged','loud and metallic','The figurative sense extends silk’s smoothness.')]);
P('sill','Sill is an old Germanic word, recorded in Old English as syll; it names a horizontal base or ledge, especially beneath a window.',C('sill.s1','building','She set the damp flowerpot on the stone sill to catch the morning light.','她把潮湿的花盆放在石窗台上，让它沐浴晨光。','stone sill','名词指窗框底部的水平构件，常可放置物品。','The sill is the horizontal piece at the base of a window frame.','sill 是窗框底部的水平构件。'),M('The carpenter installed the sill above the window frame, where it could not support the lower edge.','The carpenter installed the sill at the base of the window frame to support its lower edge.','窗台构件位于窗框底部，不在顶部。','context'),[Q(1,'Where did she put the flowerpot?','on the horizontal ledge at the window base','on the roof ridge','inside the window glass','A sill is the ledge at the base of a window.'),Q(1,'Which part is a window sill?','the horizontal piece along the bottom of the frame','the vertical curtain','the glass pane’s centre','The source definition locates it at the base.'),Q(1,'What is a sill most likely made to do?','provide a base or ledge at a window','silence an engine','carry river sediment','The sill forms the bottom horizontal piece.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a stone window sill','a window sill singing loudly','a sill of six people','A sill is a building component, often described by material.')]);
P('silliness','Silliness is silly + -ness, the noun suffix that names a quality or instance; silly once meant “blessed, happy” in Old English before shifting toward foolishness.',[C('silliness.s1','judgement','They regretted the silliness of spending the travel budget on matching hats.','他们后悔把旅行经费用来买配套帽子的愚蠢做法。','the silliness of spending','of 短语说明缺乏判断力的行为。','The first sense is the quality of lacking good sense or judgement.','第一义指缺乏判断力的性质。'),C('silliness.s2','remarks','The children’s harmless silliness made the long wait feel shorter.','孩子们无伤大雅的傻话和胡闹让漫长等待没那么难熬。','harmless silliness','抽象名词指轻松、不严重的愚蠢言行。','The second sense is a foolish remark or action that is not serious.','第二义可指不严重的蠢话或行为。')],M('They called the silliness harmless, although it involved a serious threat to injure a child.','They called the silliness harmless because it was a playful, unserious joke.','严重伤害威胁不能当作无伤大雅的玩笑。','context'),[Q(1,'What does silliness describe in the budget example?','poor judgement in spending','the children’s height','a window ledge','The first sense is a lack of good sense.'),Q(2,'Why did the children’s silliness help?','their playful foolishness made the wait easier','they damaged the travel budget','they repaired the clock','The second sense can be harmless foolish behavior.'),Q(1,'Which is an example of silliness as poor judgement?','buying hats instead of funding the trip','laughing at a gentle joke','waiting quietly','The example with the budget shows bad judgement.'),Q(2,'A harmless bit of silliness is…','a playful, not serious action','a deliberate act of violence','a legal contract','The second sense refers to unserious foolishness.')]);
P('silly','Silly comes from Old English sælig/gesælig “happy, blessed, fortunate”; over centuries its sense shifted through innocent or simple to foolish.',[C('silly.s1','judgement','It was silly to leave the only key inside the locked cabin.','把唯一的钥匙留在锁着的小屋里，实在不明智。','silly to leave','it is + adjective + to-infinitive，评价行为判断不佳。','The adjective means showing poor judgement or common sense.','此处表示缺乏常识或判断力。'),C('silly.s2','play','The cousins wore paper crowns and made silly faces for the camera.','表兄妹戴着纸王冠，对着相机做鬼脸逗乐。','silly faces','silly 描写故意滑稽、不认真的行为。','The playful sense means not serious, done for fun.','此处是闹着玩、逗趣的意思。')],M('It was silly to lock the only key outside the cabin, so the family could enter easily.','It was silly to leave the only key inside the locked cabin, because nobody could get in.','把唯一钥匙锁在屋内会妨碍进入，行为欠考虑；“在屋外”则不构成该问题。','context'),[Q(1,'Why was leaving the key inside silly?','it left everyone unable to enter','it made the key easier to find inside','it turned the cabin into a camera','The decision shows poor judgement.'),Q(2,'What were the cousins doing with silly faces?','playing and trying to be funny','making a serious legal claim','measuring the room','The second sense is playful and not serious.'),Q(1,'Which action is silly in the judgement sense?','forgetting to bring a map on a remote hike','wearing a paper crown for a joke','laughing at a comic face','The first sense criticizes unwise judgement.'),Q(2,'A silly costume at a party is usually…','playful rather than serious','proof that someone lacks all intelligence','a window component','The adjective can describe something done for fun.')]);
P('silt','Silt is a Middle English word for fine sediment; its deeper origin is uncertain. It can name river-deposited particles or the act of filling with them.',[C('silt.s1','river','After the flood, farmers spread the fresh silt left across the fields.','洪水过后，农民把留下的细河泥铺到田地里。','fresh silt left','silt 作物质名词，指水流沉积的细颗粒土。','The noun is fine earth deposited by moving water.','名词指流水留下的极细泥沙。'),C('silt.s2','harbour','Without dredging, the harbour entrance will silt up and become too shallow for ferries.','如果不疏浚，港口入口会淤塞，浅得无法让渡轮通行。','will silt up','silt 作不及物动词，up 强调逐渐被泥沙填满。','The verb means become filled or blocked with silt.','动词表示被淤泥逐渐填满或堵塞。')],M('The harbour silts up when crews remove all fine sediment from its entrance.','The harbour silts up when fine sediment accumulates at its entrance.','清除沉积物不会造成淤塞；泥沙堆积才会使水道变浅。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the farmers spread?','fine sediment left by the flood','silk fibre','a chemical element','Silt is fine earth deposited by moving water.'),Q(2,'What will happen to the harbour?','sediment will accumulate and make it shallow','it will become a mountain','it will be silenced by a bell','To silt up is to become filled with fine sediment.'),Q(1,'Which material is silt?','fine particles deposited by a river','large sheets of woven cloth','a window-frame base','The noun refers to fine sediment.'),Q(2,'If a channel is silting up, workers may need to…','dredge out the accumulated sediment','add more mud to block it','paint a signpost','Dredging removes sediment that has filled a channel.')]);
P('silurian','Silurian was named by geologist Roderick Murchison in 1835 after the Silures, an ancient people of Wales, where he studied rocks of this period.',C('silurian.s1','geology','Silurian limestone in the Welsh gorge preserves fossils from an ancient shallow sea.','威尔士峡谷中的志留纪石灰岩保存着古代浅海的化石。','Silurian limestone','专名形容词作前置定语，指地质年代。','Silurian names a geological period of the Paleozoic, after the Ordovician and before the Devonian.','Silurian 指古生代志留纪，位于奥陶纪之后、泥盆纪之前。'),M('The Silurian rocks in the gorge formed after the Devonian period and before the Ordovician.','The Silurian rocks formed after the Ordovician and before the Devonian.','地质年代顺序应是奥陶纪、志留纪、泥盆纪。','context'),[Q(1,'Which period comes after the Ordovician and before the Devonian?','the Silurian','the Jurassic','the Cretaceous','Silurian occupies that Paleozoic position.'),Q(1,'Why were the Welsh rocks called Silurian?','the name refers to the ancient Silures of Wales','they contain modern silicon chips','the word means “silent” in Latin','Murchison named the period after a Welsh people.'),Q(1,'What might Silurian limestone preserve?','fossils from an ancient sea','a modern computer circuit','a silk ribbon','The example describes rocks from a geological period.'),Q(1,'Silurian is used here as…','an adjective for a geological period or its rocks','a verb meaning to silence','a unit meaning sixty','The source sense is belonging to the Silurian period.')]);
P('silver','Silver is Old English seolfor, from Proto-Germanic *silubrą; the deeper origin is uncertain. It names the metal, its colour, or something made of/coloured like it.',[C('silver.s1','metal','The jeweller tested the spoon and confirmed that it was solid silver.','珠宝商检测了这把勺子，确认它是纯银的。','solid silver','材料名词可表示金属本身或银制器物。','The first sense covers the shiny grey-white metal and objects made from it.','第一义指银这种金属及其制品。'),C('silver.s2','colour','The clouds turned silver when the moon rose above the ridge.','月亮升过山脊时，云层变成了银白色。','turned silver','turn + colour 表示变成该金属的颜色。','The second sense names the metal’s grey-white colour.','第二义是银白色。'),C('silver.s3','award','Nora won a silver medal in the 400-metre race.','诺拉在四百米比赛中获得了一枚银牌。','silver medal','silver 作形容词修饰 medal，表示银制或银色。','The adjective can describe something made of silver or having its colour.','形容词可表示银制或银色的。')],M('Nora won a silver medal, which means the award was made of bright blue plastic.','Nora won a silver medal, an award made of or coloured like silver.','silver medal 表示银制或银色奖牌，不是蓝色塑料。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the jeweller confirm?','the spoon was made of silver','the spoon was made of silk','the spoon was a rock period','Silver can name the metal used to make an object.'),Q(2,'What colour did the clouds become?','grey-white like the metal','bright green','transparent and colourless','The colour sense comes from silver’s appearance.'),Q(3,'What does silver medal describe?','a medal made of silver or silver-coloured','a medal that silences an engine','a medal measuring one metre','The adjective describes material or colour.'),Q(1,'Which statement is accurate?','silver can name a metal, a colour, or describe an object','silver is the symbol for silica','silver always means the number six','The source entry includes noun and adjective senses.')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('silversmith','Silversmith is a transparent compound of silver and smith; smith is Old English smið, a worker who shapes metal.',C('silversmith.s1','craft','The silversmith chased a delicate vine pattern into the silver bowl before polishing its rim.','银器匠在抛光碗沿之前，把精致的藤蔓图案錾刻在银碗上。','silversmith chased a pattern','chase 在金工中指錾刻装饰纹样。','A silversmith is a craftsperson who makes or shapes silver objects.','该词指加工银器、首饰或餐具的工匠。'),M('The silversmith shaped the silver bowl by growing it from a seed in the garden.','The silversmith shaped the silver bowl by hammering and engraving the metal.','银器匠靠加工金属制作银器，不是种植出来的。','context'),[Q(1,'What did the silversmith do to the bowl?','engraved a pattern in the silver','grew it from a seed','wove it from silk','A silversmith works silver into objects and decoration.'),Q(1,'Which craftsperson is a silversmith?','someone who makes a silver serving dish','someone who writes road signs','someone who studies only river mud','The compound names a worker in silver.'),Q(1,'What is the role of smith in silversmith?','a worker who shapes metal','a unit of time','a word meaning silent','Smith names a craft worker, here one who works silver.'),Q(1,'Which object could a silversmith make?','a silver bowl','a silicon solar cell wafer only','a silk cocoon','Silver plate and utensils are typical products.')]);
P('silvery','Silvery is silver + -y, the adjective-forming suffix; it can mean containing silver or resembling its pale shine or clear ring.',[C('silvery.s1','material','The assay showed that the silvery coating contained a small amount of real silver.','化验显示，这层银色镀层含有少量真正的银。','silvery coating contained','silvery 修饰 coating；此处指含银的材料。','The first sense describes something made of or containing silver.','第一义指由银制成或含银。'),C('silvery.s2','appearance','A silvery moonbeam crossed the lake, while a silvery bell rang from the chapel.','银白色的月光横过湖面，教堂同时传来清脆悦耳的银铃声。','silvery moonbeam; silvery bell','同一义项兼有银白光泽和清脆悦耳两种引申用法。','The second sense describes a pale silver-like shine or a clear, pleasant sound.','第二义可形容银白光泽，也可形容清脆悦耳的声音。')],M('The bell had a silvery tone: its sound was muddy, dull, and unpleasant.','The bell had a silvery tone: its sound was clear and pleasantly ringing.','silvery 用于声音时表示清脆悦耳，不是沉闷难听。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the assay discover?','the coating contained some silver','the coating was made of river silt','the coating was entirely silk','The first sense concerns actual silver content.'),Q(2,'What was the moonbeam like?','pale and shining like silver','dark and muddy','made of metal','Silvery can describe a silver-like light or colour.'),Q(2,'What did silvery describe about the bell?','its clear, pleasant ringing tone','its chemical composition as pure silver','its weight in grams','The second sense also describes a clear, pleasant sound.'),Q(1,'Which use is literal-material silvery?','a silvery alloy containing silver','a silvery laugh with a clear ring','a silvery moonlit cloud','The alloy is described by its silver content.')]);
P('similar','Similar comes through French similaire from Latin similis, “like”; the adjective indicates shared qualities without identity, or near equality in size or amount.',[C('similar.s1','comparison','The two research teams used similar methods, although they studied different rivers.','两个研究团队采用了相似的方法，尽管研究的是不同河流。','similar methods','similar 后常接 to 或名词短语，说明共同特点。','The teams share important qualities but are not identical.','此处是有相似点但不完全相同。'),C('similar.s2','measurement','The two parcels are of similar weight, so they will cost the same to ship.','两个包裹重量大致相同，因此运费会一样。','of similar weight','of + adjective + noun 表示重量接近。','This sense means almost equal in amount or measurement.','该义表示数量或尺寸大致相等。')],M('The two parcels are of similar weight: one weighs 2 kg and the other 40 kg.','The two parcels are of similar weight: each weighs about 2 kg.','2 千克与 40 千克相差悬殊，不能称为重量相近。','measurement'),[Q(1,'How were the teams alike?','they used methods with important features in common','they studied exactly the same river','they had the same members','Similar means sharing qualities without being identical.'),Q(2,'What does similar weight mean here?','almost equal weight','identical packaging','different shipping companies','The second sense refers to near equality in measurement.'),Q(1,'Which pair is most similar in method?','two studies using the same sampling steps','a field survey and a cooking recipe','two teams with no shared procedure','Similar requires meaningful shared qualities.'),Q(2,'Which phrase correctly describes near-equal sizes?','rooms of similar size','rooms similar size of','rooms at similarity size','The source example uses “of a similar size.”')]);
P('similar to','The phrase is the adjective similar followed by the preposition to; the preposition introduces the person or thing used for comparison.',C('similar to.s1','comparison','This year’s rainfall pattern is similar to last year’s, but the spring peak came earlier.','今年的降雨模式与去年相似，不过春季峰值来得更早。','similar to last year’s','similar to + comparison object；相似不表示完全相同。','The phrase marks resemblance in one or more respects while allowing differences.','该短语表示某些方面相像，同时仍可有差异。'),M('This year’s pattern is similar to last year’s, so every date and rainfall amount is exactly identical.','This year’s pattern is similar to last year’s, though some dates and amounts differ.','similar to 表示有相似点，不保证逐项完全相同。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What does the phrase compare?','this year’s rainfall pattern with last year’s','a river with a metal','two identical measurements only','Similar to introduces the comparison target.'),Q(1,'Does similar to mean exactly identical?','no; it allows differences','yes; every detail must match','only that one item is larger','Similarity does not require identity.'),Q(1,'Which completion is grammatical?','The result is similar to the earlier trial.','The result is similar from the earlier trial.','The result is similar than the earlier trial.','The adjective takes to before its comparison object.'),Q(1,'If two plans are similar to each other, they…','share some features but may differ','must be copies in every detail','cannot be compared','The phrase expresses resemblance, not identity.')]);
P('similarity','Similarity is formed from similar + -ity, a noun suffix for a state or quality; it can also name a particular point of resemblance.',[C('similarity.s1','analysis','The clearest similarity between the maps is that both mark the old canal in blue.','两张地图最明显的相似处是都用蓝色标出了旧运河。','similarity between the maps','similarity between A and B 指两者共有的相似点。','A similarity is a way in which people or things resemble each other.','similarity 指相似之处。')],M('The only similarity between the maps is that one marks the canal in blue and the other leaves it unmarked.','A clear similarity between the maps is that both mark the canal in blue.','一张标出而另一张没标出并非共同特征。','context'),[Q(1,'What is the similarity between the maps?','both show the canal in blue','both were drawn on the same day','neither contains any waterway','A similarity is a shared feature.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is natural?','a similarity between the two designs','a similarity among one design','a similarity for to the designs','The noun commonly takes between for two compared things.'),Q(1,'What does -ity contribute in similarity?','a noun naming a quality or state','a past-tense marker','a plural ending','The suffix forms an abstract noun from similar.'),Q(1,'A similarity need not mean that two things are…','identical in every respect','alike in at least one respect','comparable at all','The word can name just one point of resemblance.')]);
P('similarly','Similarly is similar + -ly; it means in a like manner, and sentence-initially it can introduce a parallel fact about another case.',[C('similarly.s1','procedure','The first sample was filtered twice; the second was similarly treated before testing.','第一份样品过滤了两次；第二份也以相同方式处理后才检测。','was similarly treated','副词修饰被动谓语 treated，表示处理方式相同。','The first sense is “in a like way.”','第一义是“以相似的方式”。'),C('similarly.s2','parallel fact','The north wing needs a new roof; similarly, the south wing needs urgent repairs.','北翼需要换新屋顶；同样，南翼也急需维修。','similarly, the south wing','句首连接副词引出另一项平行情况。','The second use says the same kind of fact is true of another case.','第二种用法表示另一对象也有同类情况。')],M('The north wing needs urgent roof repairs; similarly, the south wing has no damage and needs none.','The north wing needs urgent roof repairs; similarly, the south wing also needs repairs.','similarly 引出相平行的情况；南翼无损坏就不构成同类情况。','context'),[Q(1,'How was the second sample treated?','in the same way as the first','with no filtering at all','as a different map symbol','Similarly as an adverb describes a like manner.'),Q(2,'What does the sentence-initial similarly introduce?','a parallel repair need in the south wing','a contrast showing no repairs are needed','a definition of a sample','This use links a second comparable fact.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses similarly for manner?','The second file was similarly checked for errors.','Similarly, the train was late too.','The file similarity was blue.','The adverb modifies how the file was checked.'),Q(2,'If one classroom is crowded and similarly the other is crowded, the second…','has the same kind of condition','is guaranteed to be larger','has no relation to the first','Similarly marks a parallel condition.')]);
P('simile','Simile comes from Latin simile, “a likeness,” related to similis “like”; it is an explicit comparison, often signalled by like or as.',C('simile.s1','literature','“The moon hung like a lantern” is a simile because the comparison is stated directly.','“月亮像灯笼一样挂着”是明喻，因为比较关系被直接说出。','like a lantern','simile 明确把一物比作另一物，常使用 like 或 as。','A simile is an explicit comparison, unlike a metaphor that states identity.','明喻是明说的比较，不是把两者直接说成同一物。'),M('“The moon was a lantern” is an explicit simile because it uses the word like.','“The moon hung like a lantern” is an explicit simile because it uses like.','原句没有 like 或 as，直接认同两者更接近隐喻而非明喻。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why is “The moon hung like a lantern” a simile?','it explicitly compares the moon to a lantern','it gives the moon a chemical formula','it uses no comparison at all','A simile states a comparison directly.'),Q(1,'Which phrase most clearly signals a simile?','as quiet as snow','the quiet snow','the snow is quiet','Similes commonly use like or as to mark comparison.'),Q(1,'What distinguishes a simile from a direct metaphor?','the comparison is explicitly signalled','the simile must be about the moon','the simile always has four lines','An explicit comparison is the defining feature.'),Q(1,'Which is a simile?','Her voice rang like a silver bell.','Her voice was a bell.','Her voice rang at noon.','Like makes the comparison explicit.')]);
P('simmer','Simmer is recorded in English from the 17th century; its deeper origin is uncertain. The verb describes gentle near-boiling cooking and, figuratively, strong feelings held just below an outburst.',[C('simmer.s1','cooking','Keep the lentils at a simmer until they soften, stirring every few minutes.','把扁豆保持在微沸状态，煮到变软，每隔几分钟搅拌一次。','at a simmer','at a simmer 是低于剧烈沸腾的温和烹煮状态。','As a verb, simmer means cook gently in liquid that is almost boiling.','动词义是将食物放在将沸未沸的液体中慢煮。'),C('simmer.s2','emotion','Frustration had been simmering among the nurses since the schedule changed.','自从排班改变后，护士们的不满一直在暗中积聚。','Frustration had been simmering','情绪作主语时 simmering 比喻强烈情感被压住、尚未爆发。','The figurative verb describes a feeling that is close to breaking out.','比喻强烈情绪压着未发、接近爆发。'),C('simmer.s3','cooking state','Once the sauce reaches a simmer, lower the flame and cover the pot.','酱汁一旦微沸，就调小火并盖上锅。','reaches a simmer','simmer 作可数名词表示微沸或该烹煮阶段。','The noun names the state or period of simmering.','名词义指微沸状态或文火烹煮阶段。')],M('The chef simmered the beans by blasting them in dry, freezing air with no liquid.','The chef simmered the beans in liquid over low heat just below a boil.','simmer 是在液体中以低温慢煮，不是干冷空气处理。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How should the lentils cook?','gently in liquid just below a boil','in dry ice without any liquid','at a rolling boil that splashes out','Simmer means gentle near-boiling cooking.'),Q(2,'What was happening to the nurses’ frustration?','it was building but not yet erupting','it had vanished before the schedule changed','it was cooking in a pot','The figurative sense describes a feeling held near an outburst.'),Q(3,'What does “reaches a simmer” name?','the sauce’s gentle near-boiling state','the moment it freezes solid','the amount of lentils in the pot','Simmer can be a noun for this cooking state.'),Q(2,'Which sentence uses the emotional sense?','Resentment simmered after the unfair decision.','The soup simmered with carrots.','She reached a simmer on the stove.','Strong feelings can simmer figuratively.')]);
P('simple','Simple comes through Old French from Latin simplus, “single, uncomplicated”; source senses cover ease, plainness, and having one part rather than being compound.',[C('simple.s1','instructions','The nurse wrote a simple set of steps so a new patient could use the inhaler correctly.','护士写了一套简单明了的步骤，让新患者能正确使用吸入器。','simple set of steps','simple 修饰 steps，表示容易理解或操作。','The first sense is easy to understand, do, or use.','第一义是容易理解、操作或使用。'),C('simple.s2','lifestyle','They chose a simple wooden table with no carving or glossy finish.','他们选了一张朴素的木桌，没有雕花或亮面涂层。','simple wooden table','simple 在此强调朴素、不加装饰。','The second sense means plain, without extra decoration or luxury.','第二义指朴素、没有多余装饰。'),C('simple.s3','grammar','“Birds migrate” is a simple sentence with one independent clause.','“鸟类迁徙”是只有一个独立分句的简单句。','simple sentence','simple 描写句子只有一个分句结构。','The structural sense means having one part, not being compound.','结构义指单一、不复合。')],M('“Birds migrate” is a simple sentence because it contains three independent clauses joined together.','“Birds migrate” is a simple sentence because it contains one independent clause.','一个分句才符合这里的 simple；多个独立分句组成的是复合句。','grammar'),[Q(1,'Why were the inhaler steps simple?','a new patient could understand and follow them','they had no words or instructions','they described three unrelated devices','Simple can mean easy to understand or do.'),Q(2,'What made the table simple?','it had no carving or glossy decoration','it was impossible to use','it had four different mechanisms','The plainness sense concerns lack of ornament.'),Q(3,'How many independent clauses are in “Birds migrate”?','one','three','none; it is only a phrase','A simple sentence has one independent clause.'),Q(2,'Which item is simple in the plain-style sense?','an undecorated wooden bowl','a complex machine with many controls','a paragraph that is easy to follow','The second sense means plain rather than easy.')]);
P('simplicity','Simplicity comes from Latin simplicitas, “singleness, simplicity,” through French simplicité; it names ease or a plain, unadorned quality.',[C('simplicity.s1','design','The simplicity of the new form reduced the time needed to register each visitor.','新表格设计简明，使登记每位访客所需的时间减少了。','simplicity of the new form','of 短语说明容易填写的性质带来的效果。','The first sense is the quality of being easy to understand, use, or do.','第一义指易懂、易用或易做的性质。'),C('simplicity.s2','style','The room’s simplicity came from bare wood, white walls, and almost no decoration.','房间的朴素来自裸木、白墙和几乎没有装饰。','room’s simplicity','所有格说明朴素风格属于房间。','The second sense is a plain and natural style without ornament.','第二义指朴素自然、没有装饰。')],M('The simplicity of the form slowed registration because every field required a separate legal code.','The simplicity of the form sped registration because it used only a few clear fields.','复杂字段会削弱“易用”的简明性，不会使登记更快。','context'),[Q(1,'What effect did the form’s simplicity have?','it made visitor registration quicker','it added more legal codes','it decorated the room','Simplicity as ease makes a form easier to use.'),Q(2,'Why did the room feel simple?','it had plain materials and little decoration','it contained a confusing registration form','it had elaborate gold carvings','The second sense describes an unadorned style.'),Q(1,'What does simplicity name in the usability sense?','ease of understanding or use','the number of visitors','the color of a window sill','It is a quality of being easy to use or do.'),Q(2,'Which detail best supports simplicity as a style?','bare wood and almost no ornament','many layers of gilded carving','a long technical instruction sheet','The style sense is plain and natural.')]);
P('simplification','Simplification is formed from simplify + -ation, naming the act of making something simpler or the simpler result.',C('simplification.s1','administration','The simplification of the permit form removed two duplicate questions but kept the safety checks.','许可证表格的简化删除了两个重复问题，同时保留了安全检查。','simplification of the permit form','of 短语指降低表格复杂度的行为或结果。','A simplification reduces complexity or names the simpler form produced.','simplification 指降低复杂度的行为或其结果。'),M('The simplification of the form made it longer and added several duplicate sections.','The simplification of the form shortened it by removing duplicate sections.','增加重复部分使表格更复杂，不是简化。','word-formation'),[Q(1,'What did the simplification remove?','two duplicate questions','all safety checks','the permit itself','The example reduces complexity while preserving essential checks.'),Q(1,'Simplification can name…','the act of reducing complexity or its result','a person who signs a permit','a period of near-boiling cooking','The noun covers both process and outcome.'),Q(1,'Which change is a simplification?','combining repeated fields into one clear question','adding three confusing steps','replacing a short form with a longer duplicate','Simplification removes unnecessary complexity.'),Q(1,'What does -ation do in simplification?','forms a noun for an action or result','marks a plural verb','means the opposite of simple','The ending creates an action/result noun from simplify.')]);
P('simplify','Simplify came through French simplifier, from simple + a verb-forming element meaning “make”; it means make easier to understand/do or remove needless parts for efficiency.',[C('simplify.s1','teaching','The tutor simplified the ratio problem by drawing a small diagram beside the numbers.','导师在数字旁画了一个小图，把比例题讲得更容易理解。','simplified the ratio problem','simplify + object 表示让内容更容易理解。','The first sense makes something easier to understand or do.','第一义是让事情更容易理解或完成。'),C('simplify.s2','business','The clinic simplified its booking system by merging three overlapping appointment queues.','诊所把三个重叠的预约队列合并，从而精简了预约系统。','simplified its booking system','by + -ing 说明删除多余部分、提高效率的方式。','The second sense removes unnecessary parts so a system works more efficiently.','第二义是去掉冗余以提高效率。')],M('The clinic simplified its booking system by adding four duplicate queues and more forms.','The clinic simplified its booking system by merging duplicate queues and removing redundant forms.','增加重复队列让流程更繁琐，不是简化。','context'),[Q(1,'How did the tutor simplify the ratio problem?','by adding a diagram that made it easier to understand','by hiding the numbers','by introducing a harder theorem','The first sense is making a task easier to understand.'),Q(2,'What improved the clinic’s system?','merging overlapping queues','adding more duplicate queues','removing all appointments','The second sense improves efficiency by removing unnecessary parts.'),Q(1,'Which action simplifies instructions?','rewriting them in clear steps for beginners','adding unexplained abbreviations','making each step longer and duplicated','Simplify can make instructions easier to follow.'),Q(2,'What does simplify mean in “simplify its product range”?','remove unnecessary options for efficiency','make each product more complicated','write an easier definition only','The second sense is streamlining a system or range.')]);
P('simplistic','Simplistic combines simple with -istic; the suffix gives an adjective, often with a critical sense that an account is too simple for a complex issue.',C('simplistic.s1','argument','Calling poverty a matter of laziness is a simplistic explanation that ignores wages, housing, and health.','把贫困说成懒惰造成，是一种过分简单化的解释，因为它忽视了工资、住房和健康因素。','simplistic explanation','形容词批评解释未反映复杂现实。','Simplistic means too simple to account for a genuinely complicated subject.','simplistic 指简单得未能体现事情的复杂性。'),M('The report’s simplistic account of climate risk carefully weighs many interacting causes and uncertainties.','The report’s nuanced account of climate risk weighs many interacting causes and uncertainties.','若分析认真衡量多重因素，就不应称其 simplistic。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why is the poverty explanation simplistic?','it ignores several interacting causes','it discusses wages, housing, and health in detail','it uses a diagram','Simplistic describes an account too simple for the real complexity.'),Q(1,'Which description fits a simplistic answer?','it reduces a complex issue to one unsupported cause','it compares evidence from many sources','it carefully notes uncertainty','The word is often critical of oversimplification.'),Q(1,'How does simplistic differ from simple?','simplistic often criticizes excessive oversimplification','simplistic always means easy to use','simple is always a negative judgement','The suffix and usage give simplistic a critical nuance.'),Q(1,'What would make a policy analysis less simplistic?','considering several interacting causes','ignoring all evidence but one slogan','removing every qualification','Complex analysis accounts for more than one factor.')]);
P('simply','Simply is simple + -ly; it can mean in an easy manner, only/nothing more than, or serve as an intensifier meaning completely.',[C('simply.s1','explanation','The guide explained the water filter simply, using a clean diagram and everyday words.','指南用清晰的图和日常用语简单明了地解释了净水器。','explained ... simply','simply 修饰 explained，说明表达方式容易理解。','The first sense is in a way that is easy to understand or do.','第一义是简单易懂地。'),C('simply.s2','limitation','We simply need one more signature before the permit can be issued.','许可证签发前，我们只需要再有一个签名。','simply need one more','simply 表示 only/nothing more than，限制所需数量。','The second sense means only or no more than.','第二义是仅仅、只不过。'),C('simply.s3','emphasis','The proposed bridge is simply too narrow for two buses to pass safely.','拟建的桥实在太窄，两辆公交车无法安全会车。','simply too narrow','simply 在此加强 too narrow 的程度。','The third sense emphasizes that a statement is completely true.','第三义用来加强判断，表示确实、简直。')],M('We simply need one signature, but the clerk says we need exactly twelve more.','We simply need one more signature, and no additional document is required.','simply 表示只需一个签名；再要十二个与此限制不符。','meaning'),[Q(1,'How did the guide explain the filter?','in an easy-to-understand way','only one time','too narrowly for buses','The adverb modifies the manner of explaining.'),Q(2,'What does simply mean in “simply need one more”?','only','completely impossible','in a complicated manner','This use limits the requirement to one additional signature.'),Q(3,'What does simply add in “simply too narrow”?','emphasis that it is indeed too narrow','a count of exactly one bridge','a comparison to a water filter','The intensifier strengthens the judgement.'),Q(2,'Which paraphrase fits “We simply need a key”?','We need only a key.','We need a key in a simple shape.','We need a key that is too narrow.','Simply can mean only or nothing more than.')]);
P('simulate','Simulate comes from Latin simulare, “imitate, represent, pretend,” related to similis “like”; it can reproduce real conditions or feign a feeling.',[C('simulate.s1','training','The flight software simulates crosswinds so pilots can practise landing safely.','飞行软件模拟侧风，让飞行员练习安全着陆。','simulates crosswinds','simulate + object 指再现真实条件供训练使用。','The first sense reproduces conditions of a real process for study or practice.','第一义是再现真实过程条件，以供研究或训练。'),C('simulate.s2','behaviour','The witness simulated surprise, although she had already read the report.','这名证人假装惊讶，尽管她已经读过报告。','simulated surprise','simulate + emotion 表示假装表现出某种感受。','The second sense means pretend to have a feeling or condition.','第二义是装出某种感情或状况。')],M('The witness simulated surprise by genuinely learning the news for the first time and reacting without pretending.','The witness simulated surprise by pretending to be astonished after already learning the news.','simulation requires an imitation or pretence; a genuine first reaction is not simulated.','distinction'),[Q(1,'What does the flight software reproduce?','crosswind conditions for pilot practice','a real storm inside the cockpit','the pilots’ salaries','Simulate can reproduce conditions for training.'),Q(2,'Why was the witness’s surprise simulated?','she pretended after already reading the report','she had never heard the news','the software created a crosswind','The second sense is to feign a feeling.'),Q(1,'Which activity simulates a real process?','a computer model reproducing an aircraft landing','a report listing a pilot’s name','a window sill supporting a pot','Simulation reproduces real conditions for study or practice.'),Q(2,'To simulate confidence is to…','act as if one feels confident','measure confidence in metres','remove confidence from a computer','The verb can mean pretend to have a condition.')]);
P('simulated','Simulated is the past participle of simulate, also used as an adjective for something made to resemble the real thing or for a feigned response.',[C('simulated.s1','training','The trainees practised in a simulated cockpit with working controls but no aircraft around them.','学员们在一个操控装置可用、但周围没有真实飞机的模拟驾驶舱中练习。','simulated cockpit','simulated 作前置定语，指按真实驾驶舱仿造的训练环境。','The first sense describes an imitation made to look or act like a real version.','第一义表示仿造得像真实事物的。'),C('simulated.s2','emotion','Her simulated concern disappeared as soon as the cameras were switched off.','摄像机一关，她假装出来的关心立刻消失了。','simulated concern','过去分词形容词修饰 concern，说明感情并非真实。','The second sense means not real but performed as if real, sometimes deceptively.','第二义指并非真实却装得像真的，有时带欺骗性。')],M('The simulated cockpit was the actual aircraft in flight, with no training imitation involved.','The simulated cockpit reproduced an aircraft’s controls for training on the ground.','simulated 描述仿真环境，不是实际飞行中的飞机。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What made the cockpit simulated?','it imitated an aircraft cockpit for ground training','it was an aircraft flying in the sky','it had no controls','The first sense describes a realistic imitation.'),Q(2,'What happened to the concern after filming?','the feigned concern disappeared','the training cockpit took off','the concern became a real medical condition','Simulated concern is performed rather than genuinely felt.'),Q(1,'Which is a simulated environment?','a flight-deck replica used by trainees','the real aircraft during a passenger flight','a printed word list','The adjective can describe a training imitation.'),Q(2,'A simulated smile may be…','performed without genuine happiness','a chemical element','a completely natural, involuntary response only','The second sense can describe a feigned emotion.')]);
P('simulation','Simulation comes through French from Latin simulationem, “imitation, feigning,” from simulare; it names a modelled real situation or an acted, unreal feeling.',[C('simulation.s1','training','The harbour simulation lets emergency crews practise an evacuation before a real storm arrives.','港口模拟演练让应急人员能在真正风暴来临前练习疏散。','harbour simulation','simulation 表示仿真场景或演练，供人员预先练习。','The first noun sense is an imitation of a real situation, often by computer or exercise.','第一义是对真实情形的模拟，常由计算机或演练实现。'),C('simulation.s2','behaviour','The committee saw his apology as a simulation of regret rather than genuine remorse.','委员会认为他的道歉只是对悔意的假装，而不是真正懊悔。','simulation of regret','of 短语说明被装出来的感情。','The second sense is behaviour that imitates a feeling the person does not have.','第二义是装出自己并无的感情。')],M('The harbour simulation was a computer exercise that copied a real evacuation scenario, but the note calls it an actual storm.','The harbour simulation was a computer exercise that modelled an evacuation scenario.','simulation 是演练或模型，不是实际发生的风暴。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What does the harbour simulation allow crews to do?','practise an evacuation before a real storm','evacuate only after the storm has passed','repair a silver bowl','A simulation imitates a real situation for practice.'),Q(2,'Why did the committee distrust the apology?','it seemed to imitate regret without genuine remorse','it used a computer model','it happened during a real storm','The second sense is feigned emotion.'),Q(1,'Which is a simulation?','a computer model of a flood evacuation','the flood itself','a promise made in silence','A model or exercise can imitate a real situation.'),Q(2,'“A simulation of regret” suggests…','an acted feeling that may not be genuine','a measure of river sediment','an exact expression of real remorse','The noun can mean feigning a feeling.')]);
P('simultaneous','Simultaneous comes from Latin simultaneus, from simul “at the same time”; the adjective describes events or states that occur together.',C('simultaneous.s1','events','The simultaneous alarms from both buildings confused the control-room staff.','两栋楼同时响起警报，让控制室工作人员一时不知所措。','simultaneous alarms','形容词修饰 alarms，说明两处警报在同一时刻发生。','Simultaneous means happening or existing at the same moment.','simultaneous 表示在同一时刻发生或存在。'),M('The two alarms were simultaneous because one rang at noon and the other rang three hours later.','The two alarms were simultaneous because they rang at the same moment.','相隔三小时的事件并非同时发生。','meaning'),[Q(1,'When did the two alarms sound?','at the same moment','three hours apart','one before either building existed','Simultaneous events occur at the same time.'),Q(1,'Which pair is simultaneous?','two cameras flash together','one meeting ends before another begins','a bell rings tomorrow after today’s bell','Simultaneous means happening together in time.'),Q(1,'What does the adjective modify in the example?','the alarms','the staff’s confusion only','the room’s size','It describes when the alarms occurred.'),Q(1,'Which paraphrase fits simultaneous?','occurring at the same moment','occurring in a fixed sequence','having similar colour','The adjective is temporal, not merely about resemblance.')]);
P('simultaneously','Simultaneously is simultaneous + -ly; it is an adverb meaning at the same time as another event or action.',C('simultaneously.s1','performance','The two dancers lifted their arms simultaneously on the final beat.','两名舞者在最后一拍同时举起双臂。','lifted their arms simultaneously','副词修饰 lifted，说明动作时间重合。','The adverb means at the same time.','该副词表示同时地。'),M('The dancers moved simultaneously, with one waiting until the other had finished the entire sequence.','The dancers moved simultaneously, beginning the sequence at the same moment.','一个人等另一个完成后才开始，属于先后而非同时。','meaning'),[Q(1,'When did the dancers lift their arms?','on the same final beat','one after the other in separate performances','only after the music stopped','Simultaneously describes actions occurring at the same time.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses simultaneously correctly?','The sensors recorded both temperatures simultaneously.','The sensors recorded one temperature next week simultaneously.','The sensors simultaneously were two different rooms.','The adverb modifies recording that happened together.'),Q(1,'What does simultaneously tell us?','the timing of two actions overlaps','the actions are similar in colour','the dancers are related','It means at the same time.'),Q(1,'Which is the opposite timing?','one action finishes before the other begins','two bells ring together','two lights flash at once','Simultaneous actions overlap in time, unlike a sequence.')]);
P('sin','Sin is Old English synn, a Germanic word whose deeper origin is uncertain; it names a religious offence or serious moral wrong and can also be a verb.',[C('sin.s1','ethics','In the story, the monk calls deliberate betrayal a sin because it violates his faith’s moral law.','故事中，修士称蓄意背叛为罪，因为这违反了其信仰的道德戒律。','a sin because it violates','sin 作名词，指宗教所视为冒犯神的行为或严重过错。','The noun refers to a religious offence or serious moral wrong.','名词指宗教罪过或严重道德过失。'),C('sin.s2','conduct','The character sinned by breaking the vow he had made before the community.','这个人物违背了自己在团体面前立下的誓言，因此犯了过错。','sinned by breaking','sin 作动词，by + -ing 说明违反了哪条道德规则。','As a verb, it means break a religious or moral rule.','动词表示违反宗教或道德规则。')],M('He sinned by keeping every promise and following the moral rule exactly.','He sinned by breaking the moral rule and betraying his promise.','遵守规则并信守承诺不是犯错或犯罪过。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the monk call betrayal a sin?','it violated a moral law in his faith','it happened at the same time as an alarm','it was a type of window frame','The noun can mean a religious offence or serious moral wrong.'),Q(2,'How did the character sin?','by breaking a vow','by following the vow exactly','by silently reading a book','The verb means break a moral or religious rule.'),Q(1,'Which act could be called a sin in a religious teaching?','deliberately violating a sacred rule','measuring a room','cooking lentils gently','Sin names an offence against religious or moral law.'),Q(2,'What is the verb sense of sin?','to commit a moral or religious wrong','to compare two events','to make a word simpler','The verb is to break a moral rule.')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('since','Since developed from Middle English syns/sithens, ultimately related to Old English siððan “after that”; it marks a starting time, a reason, or the period after a known time.',[C('since.s1','time','I have kept the field notes since the first survey in April.','从四月第一次调查以来，我一直保存着这些野外记录。','since the first survey','现在完成时与 since 引出的过去起点连用。','The preposition marks a past starting point continuing to a later time.','介词义标明持续到后来的过去起点。'),C('since.s2','reason','Since the bridge is closed, the bus will use the eastern road.','既然桥封闭了，公交车就改走东边的道路。','Since the bridge is closed','句首 since 引导原因从句。','The conjunction can mean because or given that.','连词义为“因为、既然”。'),C('since.s3','time','The museum opened in June, and the curator has worked there ever since.','博物馆六月开放，馆长从那以后一直在那里工作。','ever since','句末副词指从已知时间点起直到现在。','The adverb means from that known past time until now.','副词义表示从那个已知时间起至今。')],M('Since the bridge is closed, the bus will continue across it on the usual route.','Since the bridge is closed, the bus will take the eastern road instead.','原因从句既然说明桥已封闭，结果就不应仍沿桥通行。','context'),[Q(1,'Since when have the notes been kept?','from the first April survey onward','only after the museum opened','because the bridge is closed','The preposition introduces the past starting point.'),Q(2,'Why will the bus use the eastern road?','because the bridge is closed','because the notes were surveyed','since it is a later date only','Here since means because or given that.'),Q(3,'What does ever since refer to?','from June until the present','before the museum opened','a reason for closing the bridge','The adverb means from that known point until now.'),Q(2,'Which clause uses since to give a reason?','Since the road flooded, we postponed the trip.','I have lived here since 2021.','They moved in May and have stayed since.','The first clause gives the reason for the decision.')]);
P('sincere','Sincere comes from Latin sincerus, “whole, clean, pure”; its deeper origin is uncertain, and the popular “without wax” story is not established.',[C('sincere.s1','communication','Please accept our sincere thanks for returning the archive boxes intact.','请接受我们诚挚的谢意，感谢您完好归还档案箱。','sincere thanks','sincere 修饰 thanks，强调感谢发自内心而非客套。','The first sense is expressing what one really feels without pretence.','第一义是没有伪装地表达真实感受。'),C('sincere.s2','character','Even after the disagreement, Mei remained a sincere friend who did not flatter either side.','即使意见不合，梅仍是一位真诚的朋友，不会奉承任何一方。','sincere friend','形容词作 friend 前置定语，说明此人的待人方式。','The person sense describes someone who does not pretend feelings to please others.','指不为取悦他人而假装感情的人。')],M('His sincere apology was designed only to flatter the panel, and he admitted he did not mean a word of it.','His insincere apology was designed only to flatter the panel, and he admitted he did not mean a word of it.','若当事人承认只是奉承且并不真心，sincere 就不准确。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why were the thanks sincere?','they expressed genuine gratitude','they were copied from a false excuse','they hid a request for money','Sincere means genuinely felt, not pretended.'),Q(2,'What made Mei a sincere friend?','she did not flatter either side','she changed her feelings to please everyone','she returned archive boxes','The person sense concerns honest feeling.'),Q(1,'Which statement is accurate about the word’s origin?','it comes from Latin sincerus; the “without wax” story is unproven','it certainly means “without wax” in Latin','it was formed from silicon and silver','The supposed wax explanation is folk etymology, not established history.'),Q(1,'Which phrase is most natural?','a sincere expression of thanks','a sincere metal window sill','a sincere amount of river silt','Sincere describes genuine feeling or intention.')]);
P('sincerely','Sincerely is sincere + -ly; it means honestly or genuinely, and it is also used in the conventional closing “Yours sincerely” in formal letters.',[C('sincerely.s1','honesty','I sincerely hope the injured hikers recover fully after the rescue.','我真诚地希望受伤的徒步者获救后能完全康复。','sincerely hope','副词修饰 hope，强调愿望真实而非敷衍。','The first sense means in an honest, genuine way.','第一义表示真诚地、发自内心地。'),C('sincerely.s2','letter writing','After naming the recipient, the editor closed the formal letter with “Yours sincerely”.','写明收信人后，编辑在正式信函末尾写上“谨上”。','closed the formal letter with','该用法是正式信函的固定结尾，放在署名前。','The second sense is a conventional sign-off in a formal letter.','第二义是正式信函中的结尾敬语。')],M('The editor began the letter with “Yours sincerely” as the salutation before naming the recipient.','The editor ended the letter with “Yours sincerely” before signing the name.','Yours sincerely 是结尾敬语，放在正文后、署名前，不是称呼语。','usage'),[Q(1,'What does the writer genuinely hope?','that the hikers recover fully','that the rescue is cancelled','that the letter is unsigned','Sincerely modifies hope to mark a genuine wish.'),Q(2,'Where does “Yours sincerely” appear?','at the end of a formal letter before the signature','as the first greeting before the recipient’s name','in the middle of every sentence','It is a conventional letter closing.'),Q(1,'Which use expresses honest feeling?','I sincerely appreciate your help.','Yours sincerely, at the top of a letter','The room is sincerely six metres wide.','The adverb can mean genuinely or honestly.'),Q(2,'What is the function of the closing phrase?','a formal sign-off before the sender’s name','a greeting before the letter body','a measurement of honesty','The phrase is used at the end of a formal letter.')]);
P('sincerity','Sincerity comes through French sincérité from Latin sinceritas, “purity, soundness”; it names honesty of intention and freedom from deceit.',C('sincerity.s1','trust','The mediator questioned the sincerity of the offer because its terms changed whenever the other side agreed.','调解员怀疑这项提议是否真诚，因为对方每次同意后条款都会改变。','sincerity of the offer','sincerity 常与 of 连用，说明某种表态是否出于诚意。','Sincerity is honest intention without deception.','sincerity 指诚实的用意、不含欺骗。'),M('The mediator trusted the offer’s sincerity because the negotiator secretly admitted it was a deliberate lie.','The mediator doubted the offer’s sincerity because the negotiator admitted it was a deliberate lie.','蓄意撒谎与诚意相反。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the mediator question the offer’s sincerity?','its terms shifted after each agreement','it was written on white paper','the meeting happened in April','Changing terms suggested the offer might not be honest.'),Q(1,'Sincerity is closest to…','honesty of intention','a soundproofing device','a mathematical fraction','The noun concerns genuine, non-deceptive intention.'),Q(1,'Which behavior shows sincerity?','keeping a promise even when it is inconvenient','pretending to agree while planning to deceive','changing a claim whenever challenged','Sincerity excludes deliberate deceit.'),Q(1,'What does “doubt the sincerity of an apology” mean?','question whether the apology is genuine','ask how long the apology lasts','measure the apology’s volume','Sincerity concerns whether feelings or intentions are genuine.')]);
P('sinew','Sinew is Old English seonowe, “tendon”; its deeper Germanic history is uncertain. The word also extends metaphorically to the strength or resources that make something work.',[C('sinew.s1','anatomy','The surgeon repaired a torn sinew that connects the calf muscle to the heel.','外科医生修复了一条撕裂的肌腱，它把小腿肌肉连到脚跟。','sinew that connects','关系从句说明肌腱连接肌肉和骨骼。','A sinew is a tough cord or tendon attaching muscle to bone.','sinew 指把肌肉连到骨头上的坚韧肌腱。'),C('sinew.s2','figurative','Local volunteers are the sinews of the festival, providing the energy that keeps it running.','当地志愿者是节庆活动的支柱，提供维持活动运转的力量。','sinews of the festival','复数比喻义与 of 连用，表示不可或缺的力量或资源。','Figuratively, sinew means strength or resources needed to sustain an effort.','比喻义表示支撑一项事业所需的力量或资源。')],M('The volunteers were the sinews of the festival because they weakened every activity and removed all support.','The volunteers were the sinews of the festival because their effort kept it running.','比喻义的 sinews 是支撑活动的力量，不是削弱因素。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the surgeon repair?','a tendon linking muscle to bone','a silver window sill','a type of river mud','The anatomical sense is a tough tendon.'),Q(2,'Why were volunteers called the sinews of the festival?','they supplied the strength that sustained it','they were the event’s decorations','they were all injured runners','The figurative sense is vital strength or resources.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses sinew literally?','A sinew was torn in the runner’s calf.','The sinew of the campaign was public support.','The river left a layer of silt.','A torn calf tendon is the literal sense.'),Q(2,'In “the sinews of the economy,” sinews are…','the resources and strength that keep it functioning','the bones of every worker','a count of the number of businesses','The metaphor names supporting strength.')]);
P('sinful','Sinful is sin + -ful, “full of or characterized by sin”; it can mean violating moral/religious rules or, more strongly, shockingly wicked.',[C('sinful.s1','religion','The monk described deliberate cruelty as sinful because it violated the teaching’s moral rules.','修士称蓄意残忍为有罪，因为它违反了教义的道德准则。','described ... as sinful','describe A as B 说明行为符合道德或宗教意义上的罪过。','The first sense means breaking a rule of right and wrong, especially a religious rule.','第一义指违背道德或宗教戒律。'),C('sinful.s2','moral judgement','The novel portrays the ruler’s sinful cruelty as so shocking that even his allies abandon him.','小说把统治者邪恶残忍的行径描写得骇人听闻，连盟友也抛弃了他。','sinful cruelty','sinful 加强道德谴责，形容令人震惊的恶行。','The second sense is deeply wrong or wicked in a way that shocks people.','第二义指邪恶败坏得令人震惊。')],M('The ruler’s sinful cruelty was admired as a harmless act of kindness that hurt nobody.','The ruler’s sinful cruelty was condemned as deeply wrong and harmful.','残酷伤害他人与无害善行相矛盾；sinful 在此是强烈道德谴责。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why was the cruelty called sinful?','it broke a moral rule in the teaching','it was a form of gentle cooking','it made a room silent','The first sense concerns violation of a moral or religious rule.'),Q(2,'How does the novel present the ruler’s cruelty?','as shocking and deeply wicked','as an ordinary neutral choice','as a mathematical fraction','The stronger sense is morally outrageous.'),Q(1,'What does -ful contribute to sinful?','characterized by or full of sin','one who removes sin','the past tense of sin','The suffix -ful forms an adjective meaning full of/characterized by.'),Q(2,'Which behavior is most likely called sinful in the stronger sense?','deliberately abusing helpless people','politely disagreeing about a book','measuring a window sill','The stronger sense describes shocking wrongdoing.')]);
P('sing','Sing is Old English singan, from Proto-Germanic *singwaną; it means make music with the voice, produce a musical call, or enthusiastically praise.',[C('sing.s1','music','The choir sang a lullaby softly while the children settled into bed.','孩子们准备入睡时，合唱团轻轻唱了一首摇篮曲。','sang a lullaby','sing + song 作宾语，表示用嗓音演唱。','The first sense is to make music with the voice.','第一义是用嗓音唱歌。'),C('sing.s2','animals','A blackbird sang from the hedge just before sunrise.','日出前，一只乌鸫在树篱上鸣唱。','blackbird sang','动物作主语时 sing 表示发出高而悦耳的声音。','Birds and similar sources can sing by producing a musical sound.','鸟等也可用 sing 表示发出悦耳的鸣声。'),C('sing.s3','praise','The review sang the praises of the small theatre for making room for new writers.','评论热情赞扬这家小剧院为新作家提供了机会。','sang the praises of','固定搭配 sing the praises of 表示热情赞扬。','The third sense means praise someone or something enthusiastically.','第三义是热情赞扬。')],M('The review sang the theatre’s praises while calling its work worthless and urging readers to avoid it.','The review sang the theatre’s praises by enthusiastically describing its support for new writers.','sing someone’s praises 表示热情赞扬，不能同时用完全贬低的评价。','context'),[Q(1,'What did the choir sing?','a lullaby','a map symbol','a legal rule','The first sense is musical singing with the voice.'),Q(2,'What was the blackbird doing?','making a musical call','praising the theatre','simmering in a pot','Birds can sing in the sense of making a musical sound.'),Q(3,'What does the review do in “sang the praises”?','praise the theatre enthusiastically','perform a lullaby','describe a bird call','The phrase means to speak warmly in praise of something.'),Q(3,'Which phrase uses sing as praise?','The article sang the praises of the library.','The choir sang a hymn.','The bird sang at dawn.','Only the first phrase means praise.')]);
P('singe','Singe is Old English sencgan, “to burn slightly”; it means burn only the surface of hair, cloth, or food without destroying the whole.',C('singe.s1','cooking','The cook singed the pepper skin over a flame, then peeled off the blackened surface.','厨师在火上轻轻烧焦甜椒皮，随后剥掉烧黑的表层。','singed the pepper skin','singe 表示表面轻微烧焦，后续仍可剥掉使用。','The verb burns an outer surface without consuming the whole object.','动词指只烧焦外层而不把整体烧毁。'),M('The candle singed the curtain by reducing the entire fabric to cold ash.','The candle singed the curtain by scorching a small patch of its outer fibres.','singe 是局部表层轻度灼焦，不是把整块布烧成灰。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What happened to the pepper skin?','its outer surface was lightly scorched','the whole pepper was reduced to ash','it was frozen solid','Singe means burn the surface slightly.'),Q(1,'Which action singes hair?','briefly scorching a few outer hairs','burning a whole person completely','washing hair with cold water','The verb describes a light surface burn.'),Q(1,'What did the candle do to the curtain?','scorched a small patch of outer fibres','turned all fabric into ash','made the curtain silvery','Singe does not mean destroy the whole fabric.'),Q(1,'Which correction best preserves the intended meaning?','The cook singed the skin before peeling it.','The cook sank the skin below water.','The cook sang the skin to sleep.','Singe fits a slight surface burn.')]);
P('singer','Singer is sing + -er, the agent suffix naming someone who sings, professionally or in a particular style.',[C('singer.s1','music','The singer remembered every verse during the live performance, even when the monitor failed.','现场演出时，监听设备失灵，但歌手仍记得每一段歌词。','the singer remembered','agent noun names the person who performs songs.','A singer is a person who sings, often as a job or in a band.','singer 指唱歌的人，常以此为职业或在乐队演唱。'),C('singer.s2','ability','Although he rarely performs, he is a confident singer of traditional sea shanties.','虽然他很少登台，但他唱传统海上船歌很有把握。','singer of traditional sea shanties','of 短语指出其擅长演唱的风格。','The word can specify a person who sings in a particular way or style.','该词也可指擅长某种唱法或风格的人。')],M('The singer performed the song without using a voice, instrument, or recorded track.','The singer performed the song using her voice on stage.','singer 指唱歌的人；完全不用声音或录音就不能称为演唱。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What did the singer do despite the monitor failure?','remembered the verses during the performance','repaired the stage roof','wrote the word on a signpost','A singer performs songs with the voice.'),Q(2,'What kind of singer is the man?','someone who sings traditional sea shanties confidently','someone who only repairs ships','someone who never sings','The second sense can specify a style of singing.'),Q(1,'Which person is a singer?','a person performing songs with the voice','a person drawing a silhouette only','a person measuring sixteenth parts','Singer names someone who sings.'),Q(2,'What does “a singer of sea shanties” tell us?','the style of songs the person sings','the person’s exact height','that the person is a ship’s silencer','The phrase identifies a repertoire or singing style.')]);
P('singing','Singing is sing + -ing; as a noun it names the activity or skill of making music vocally and can also mean the sound a person or animal produces.',[C('singing.s1','skill','After taking weekly singing lessons, Omar learned to control his breathing through long phrases.','每周上声乐课后，奥马尔学会了在长乐句中控制呼吸。','singing lessons','singing 作活动/技能名词，是课程内容。','The first sense is the activity or skill of making musical sounds with the voice.','第一义是用人声演唱的活动或技能。'),C('singing.s2','sound','The blackbird’s singing woke the campers before the sun appeared.','太阳出来前，乌鸫的鸣唱就把露营者叫醒了。','blackbird’s singing','所有格修饰 singing，指鸟唱出的声音。','The second sense is the sound made by a person, bird, or insect when singing.','第二义是人、鸟或虫唱出的声音。')],M('Omar took singing lessons to improve his violin bowing, without ever using his voice.','Omar took singing lessons to improve his vocal control and phrasing.','singing lessons训练人声歌唱，不是弓弦演奏。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What did Omar practise in the lessons?','vocal breathing through musical phrases','bowing a violin','building a window sill','Singing as an activity uses the voice.'),Q(2,'What woke the campers?','the sound made by the blackbird','a lesson about breathing','a silent letter','Singing can name the sound an animal makes.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses singing for the activity?','a course in singing','the bird’s singing filled the dawn','the singing of a kettle’s whistle','The activity/skill sense refers to learning to sing.'),Q(2,'Which is singing in the sound sense?','the clear notes heard from a bird','a person’s weekly vocal lesson','a list of song titles','The second sense is the audible sound itself.')]);
P('single','Single comes from Old French sengle and Latin singulus, “one, individual”; it can mean one, unmarried, a one-way ticket/song/game, or select one item.',[C('single.s1','quantity','Not a single tree was left standing after the storm crossed the ridge.','风暴越过山脊后，一棵树都没有留下。','not a single tree','not a single 强调一个也没有。','The first sense means only one or not a pair/group.','第一义指单独一个、只有一个。'),C('single.s2','relationship','After her divorce, she remained single for several years and focused on her work.','离婚后，她多年保持单身，专心工作。','remained single','single 作表语形容词，描述婚恋状态。','The second sense means not married or not in a romantic partnership.','第二义是未婚或没有恋爱伴侣。'),C('single.s3','travel','We bought a single to York and planned to return by coach the next day.','我们买了去约克的单程票，计划第二天坐长途客车回来。','bought a single to York','英式交通语境中 single 可指单程票。','The noun can mean a one-way ticket; it also names a song or one-player-per-side game.','名词义可指单程票，也可指单曲或单打。'),C('single.s4','selection','The editor singled out one paragraph for special revision.','编辑挑出一个段落作特别修改。','singled out one paragraph','single 作动词短语 single out，意为从群体中挑出。','The verb means choose one member of a group for special attention.','动词义是从一组中挑出一个特别对待。')],M('The editor singled out one paragraph by revising every paragraph equally and choosing none for special attention.','The editor singled out one paragraph by choosing it for special revision.','single out 指特别挑选一个，而非平均修改所有内容。','usage'),[Q(1,'What does not a single tree mean?','not one tree','exactly two trees','every tree survived','Single can emphasize one individual item.'),Q(2,'What is her relationship status?','not married or partnered','travelling one way','a selected paragraph','Single can describe an unmarried person.'),Q(3,'What ticket did they buy?','a one-way ticket to York','a round-trip ticket to York and back','a concert record','A single is a one-way fare in this context.'),Q(4,'What did the editor do?','chose one paragraph for special attention','revised every paragraph equally','published a single song','Single out is to select one member of a group.')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('singleton','Singleton is formed from single with the ending -ton, probably by analogy with words such as simpleton; it names one item occurring alone.',C('singleton.s1','classification','She was the only singleton in a class otherwise made up of twins and triplets.','这个班除她之外都是双胞胎或三胞胎，她是唯一的独生子女。','the only singleton','singleton 指独自出现的一员，而非成对或成组。','A singleton is one item or person occurring alone in a group or set.','singleton 指一组中单独出现的一个人或事物。'),M('In the set of three identical pairs, each paired item is a singleton because it has a twin.','In the set of three pairs, an unpaired item would be the singleton.','singleton 是没有配对的单个成员；成对物品不是 singleton。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why was she a singleton in the class?','she was the only child without a twin or triplet','she was one of three triplets','she taught the class','A singleton occurs alone while the others are paired or grouped.'),Q(1,'Which set contains a singleton?','three matching pairs and one unpaired button','four pairs with no extra item','a single button in a sealed box only','The extra unpaired item is the singleton.'),Q(1,'What does singleton emphasize?','one item occurring alone','a group of exactly six','a person who sings professionally','The noun identifies a lone member.'),Q(1,'Which is a singleton in a card hand?','the one card whose rank appears only once','one of two matching queens','a complete matched pair','A singleton is an unpaired, one-off item.')]);
P('singly','Singly is single + -ly, the adverb suffix; it means one at a time or individually, rather than together.',C('singly.s1','handling','The archivist placed the brittle photographs singly into protective sleeves so they would not stick together.','档案员把易碎照片一张一张地放进保护套，以免它们粘在一起。','placed ... singly','副词修饰 placed，突出逐件处理。','Singly means individually, not as a group.','singly 表示一个一个地、各自分开地。'),M('The archivist packed the photographs singly by tying all of them into one unprotected bundle.','The archivist packed each photograph singly in its own protective sleeve.','把所有照片捆成一包不是逐张分开包装。','usage'),[Q(1,'How did the archivist place the photographs?','one at a time in separate sleeves','all tied into one bundle','in pairs inside one sleeve','Singly means individually rather than together.'),Q(1,'Which instruction means enter singly?','come through the gate one by one','arrive all together in a group','wait until every other person leaves','Singly specifies separate individual entry.'),Q(1,'Which word is the base of singly?','single','sing','sinew','The adverb is formed from single plus -ly.'),Q(1,'If seedlings are planted singly, each is…','planted individually','planted in a crowded clump','planted with a matching pair only','The adverb means separately or one at a time.')]);
P('singular','Singular comes from Latin singularis, “one, individual,” from singulus “one each”; it describes grammatical one-ness, something exceptional, or something strange.',[C('singular.s1','grammar','In the sentence “The children play,” children is plural; child is its singular form.','在句子“The children play”中，children 是复数；child 是它的单数形式。','its singular form','语法术语指表示一个人或事物的词形。','The grammatical sense is the form that refers to one person or thing.','语法义指表示一个人或事物的词形。'),C('singular.s2','achievement','The climber showed singular courage by turning back to rescue a stranger in the storm.','暴风雪中，登山者回头救陌生人，表现出非凡的勇气。','singular courage','singular 修饰抽象名词 courage，强调出众、非凡。','The second sense means very great, unusual, or excellent.','第二义指非凡、出众或极佳。'),C('singular.s3','oddity','A singular clock in the hallway rang thirteen times at midnight.','走廊里一只奇怪的钟在午夜敲了十三下。','singular clock','形容词修饰钟，指出其行为怪异。','The third sense means strange or odd.','第三义是奇怪或异常。')],M('In “The children play,” children is singular because it refers to several young people.','In “The child plays,” child is singular because it refers to one young person.','children 指多个人，是复数；child 才是单数。','grammar'),[Q(1,'What is the singular form of children?','child','children','childs','The singular grammatical form refers to one.'),Q(2,'Why was the climber’s courage singular?','it was exceptional and unusually great','it was grammatically one courage','it was strange because a clock rang','The second sense means outstanding or exceptional.'),Q(3,'Why is the clock singular in the hallway story?','it behaves in a strange, odd way','it refers to one clock in grammar only','it shows exceptional bravery','The third sense means strange.'),Q(1,'Which word is singular in “one bird sings”?','bird','birds','sing','The noun bird refers to one, while birds is plural.')]);
P('sinister','Sinister comes from Latin sinister, “left, on the left side”; Roman omen traditions associated the left with ill fortune, leading to meanings of ominous or evil.',[C('sinister.s1','atmosphere','A sinister hush fell over the empty station just before the lights went out.','灯熄灭前，一种不祥的寂静笼罩了空车站。','sinister hush','形容词修饰环境名词，制造坏事将至的感觉。','The first sense creates a feeling that something bad may happen.','第一义使人觉得坏事存在或即将发生。'),C('sinister.s2','intent','The detective noticed a sinister purpose behind the apparently generous offer.','侦探注意到这项看似慷慨的提议背后藏着险恶目的。','sinister purpose','purpose 搭配表明此处是意图邪恶、企图伤人。','The second sense suggests an evil intention or wish to harm.','第二义暗示邪恶目的或伤害他人的意图。')],M('The sinister offer had no hidden threat or harmful purpose; it was simply a transparent gift.','The sinister offer concealed a harmful purpose beneath its generous appearance.','若提议坦诚无害，就不具有 sinister 所暗示的险恶意图。','distinction'),[Q(1,'What feeling did the empty station create?','that something bad might happen','that a celebration had begun','that the room was unusually warm','Sinister can describe an ominous atmosphere.'),Q(2,'What did the detective notice?','an evil purpose behind the offer','a grammatical singular noun','a silvery bell','The intent sense suggests a wish to harm.'),Q(1,'Which scene is sinister?','a corridor where unexplained footsteps approach in darkness','a bright picnic with friends laughing','a clear map of a quiet town','The adjective often signals danger or evil.'),Q(2,'A sinister motive is…','a harmful or evil intention','a perfectly innocent plan','a person’s left shoe size','The second sense concerns malicious purpose.')]);
P('sink','Sink is Old English sincan, from Proto-Germanic *sinkwaną; it can descend below a surface, fall in level, absorb resources, or name a fixed basin.',[C('sink.s1','water','The wooden ferry began to sink after a leak opened beneath the waterline.','水线下出现破口后，木渡船开始下沉。','began to sink','不及物动词表示向水面以下沉去。','The first sense is to go below the surface of water.','第一义是沉到水面以下。'),C('sink.s2','level','After the announcement, the share price sank by six percent before recovering.','公告发布后，股价先下跌了百分之六，随后回升。','price sank by six percent','sink 用于数字或水平时表示降到较低程度。','The second sense is to fall to a lower level.','第二义表示水平下降。'),C('sink.s3','investment','They sank most of their savings into restoring the abandoned cinema.','他们把大部分积蓄投入了修复废弃电影院。','sank ... savings into','sink money/time/effort into 指投入大量资源。','The third sense means put a lot of money, time, or effort into something.','第三义是把大量金钱、时间或精力投入某事。'),C('sink.s4','kitchen','Please leave the muddy boots beside the kitchen sink, not in the pantry.','请把沾满泥的靴子放在厨房水槽旁，不要放进食品储藏室。','kitchen sink','名词表示带供水和排水设施的固定盆槽。','As a noun, a sink is a fixed basin with water supply and a drain.','名词义是有进水和排水的固定水盆。')],M('They sank their savings into the cinema by keeping every dollar in a savings account and spending none.','They sank their savings into the cinema by investing most of the money in its restoration.','把钱留在账户而不投入项目，与 sink savings into 相反。','usage'),[Q(1,'What happened to the ferry?','it went below the water surface','its price fell by six percent','it became a kitchen basin','The water sense is to descend below the surface.'),Q(2,'What happened to the share price?','it fell to a lower level','it was invested in a building','it became a fixed basin','Sink can describe a drop in a value or level.'),Q(3,'What does “sank savings into” mean?','invested a large amount of money in','washed money in a basin','lost a boat beneath water','This idiom means commit substantial resources to a project.'),Q(4,'Where should the boots be left?','beside the fixed basin in the kitchen','inside the share-price chart','under the ferry','The noun sink is a water-connected basin.')]);
P('sinkhole','Sinkhole is the compound sink + hole; in geology it names a depression created when the roof of an underground cavity collapses.',C('sinkhole.s1','geology','After days of heavy rain, a sinkhole opened beside the road where water had dissolved limestone below ground.','连续几天大雨后，地下水溶解石灰岩的路边塌出一个天坑。','sinkhole opened beside the road','名词复合词指地表凹陷，后接成因从句说明地下空洞塌陷。','A sinkhole forms when the roof of an underground cavity falls in.','sinkhole 是地下空洞顶部坍塌后形成的地表凹陷。'),M('The geologist called the flat, solid plateau with no depression a sinkhole.','The geologist called the collapsed depression above an underground cavity a sinkhole.','sinkhole 指塌陷形成的地表坑洼，而非平坦完整的高原。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What created the sinkhole beside the road?','collapse above an underground cavity','a silversmith’s hammer','a rise in the river price','Sinkholes form when an underground cavity roof falls in.'),Q(1,'Which feature is a sinkhole?','a depression where ground has collapsed','a raised metal signpost','a hole intentionally drilled in a wall only','The term names a natural ground depression.'),Q(1,'Why can limestone regions have sinkholes?','water can dissolve rock and leave cavities','limestone is made of silk','the rock sings at night','Dissolved underground rock can leave a cavity that collapses.'),Q(1,'What does the compound suggest?','a hole or depression where the ground sinks','a hole used to store a kitchen sink','a smooth silvery surface','The name transparently combines sink and hole.')]);
P('sinuous','Sinuous comes from Latin sinuosus, from sinus “curve, fold”; it describes a winding shape or a lithe, twisting movement.',C('sinuous.s1','landscape','A sinuous footpath followed the river through reeds and around three wooded bends.','一条弯弯曲曲的小路沿河穿过芦苇，又绕过三处林木茂密的河湾。','sinuous footpath','形容词强调路线不断蜿蜒转弯。','Sinuous means winding or twisting in shape.','sinuous 表示蜿蜒或扭曲的形状。'),M('The sinuous path ran in one perfectly straight line from the gate to the bridge.','The sinuous path curved repeatedly from the gate to the bridge.','笔直路线没有蜿蜒弯曲的特征。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What was the path like?','it wound around bends along the river','it ran in one straight line','it sank beneath the river','Sinuous describes a winding course.'),Q(1,'Which object is sinuous?','a twisting garden hose','a rigid ruler with no bends','a square window sill','The adjective applies to winding or twisting forms.'),Q(1,'What can sinuous describe besides a path?','a lithe, twisting movement','a person’s marital status','a unit of sixty minutes','The word may describe flexible movement.'),Q(1,'Why does Latin sinus fit the history of sinuous?','sinus means a curve or fold','sinus means “one at a time”','sinus is the Latin word for silver','Sinuous derives from a Latin word for a curve or fold.')]);
P('sip','Sip is recorded in English from the 14th century; its exact origin is uncertain, perhaps imitative. It names drinking a little at a time and the small mouthful taken.',[C('sip.s1','drinking','She sipped the hot broth slowly, testing its temperature after each small mouthful.','她慢慢啜着热汤，每小口之后都试一下温度。','sipped ... slowly','sip 作动词表示少量、分次地喝。','The verb means drink a little at a time rather than gulp.','动词表示小口喝，而非大口吞饮。'),C('sip.s2','quantity','He took one sip of the bitter medicine and then reached for water.','他只喝了一小口苦药，随后便伸手拿水。','one sip of','sip 作可数名词表示一小口饮料。','The noun is a very small amount of drink taken into the mouth.','名词义是一小口饮料。')],M('She sipped the broth by swallowing the entire bowl in one gulp without stopping.','She sipped the broth by taking small mouthfuls and pausing between them.','一次一口吞完整碗是 gulp，不是 sip。','distinction'),[Q(1,'How did she drink the broth?','in small amounts with pauses','in one large gulp','by pouring it on the table','The verb sip contrasts with gulping.'),Q(2,'How much medicine did he take?','one small mouthful','the entire bottle','a spoonful of river silt','A sip is a very small amount of drink.'),Q(1,'Which action is sipping?','tasting tea in several small mouthfuls','draining a glass in one swallow','spilling a cup without drinking','Sip means drink little by little.'),Q(2,'What does “take a sip” mean?','drink a small amount','fill a whole basin','sing a short song','The noun names a small amount of drink.')]);
P('sir','Sir came through Old French sire from Latin senior, “older”; it is a polite form of address and the title before a knight’s first name.',[C('sir.s1','politeness','“Excuse me, sir, is this seat taken?” the passenger asked the man beside the aisle.','乘客问过道旁的男子：“先生，打扰了，这个座位有人吗？”','Excuse me, sir','sir 用于礼貌称呼男子而不直呼其名。','The first sense is a polite way to address a man whose name is not used.','第一义是对不直呼其名的男子的礼貌称呼。'),C('sir.s2','honour','Sir David Attenborough narrated the documentary about the coral reef.','戴维·艾登堡爵士为这部关于珊瑚礁的纪录片担任旁白。','Sir David Attenborough','爵士头衔置于名字前，首字母大写。','The second sense is a title before the first name of a knight or baronet.','第二义是置于骑士或准男爵名字前的头衔。')],M('At the ceremony, the announcer addressed the knight as “Mr Sir David” and put Sir after his surname.','At the ceremony, the announcer introduced him as Sir David, placing Sir before his first name.','爵士头衔用在名字之前，不与 Mr 连用或放在姓后。','usage'),[Q(1,'How does the passenger use sir?','as a polite address to a man','as a title before a knight’s first name','as the name of a boat part','The first sense is respectful direct address.'),Q(2,'Why is Sir capitalized before David?','it is the title of a knight','it is the start of a question','it means any older man','The honorific title precedes the first name.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses sir as direct address?','Could you help me, sir?','Sir Isaac Newton studied physics.','The word sir is a silencer.','The first example addresses a man politely.'),Q(2,'Where does the title Sir appear?','before the knight’s first name','after the knight’s surname','only at the end of a letter','The title is placed before the first name.')]);
})();

(function(){
'use strict';
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const Q=(s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType='meaning')=>({s,prompt,answer,wrong1,wrong2,explain,errorType});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const E=(origin,w)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:`Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/${w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')}`});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistake,qs)=>D(w,{etymology:E(origin,w),contexts:Array.isArray(contexts)?contexts:[contexts],mistakes:[mistake],quiz:qs.map((q,i)=>({id:w+'.q'+(i+1),senseId:w+'.s'+q.s,prompt:q.prompt,answer:q.answer,options:[q.answer,q.wrong1,q.wrong2],explain:q.explain,errorType:q.errorType,type:'辨义与用法'}))});
P('siren','Siren comes from Latin siren and Greek Seirēn, the mythical singer who lured sailors; the modern warning device was named for its piercing, attention-drawing sound.',[C('siren.s1','emergency','The flood siren sounded three times, warning residents to move to higher ground.','洪水警报器响了三次，提醒居民转移到高处。','flood siren sounded','siren 作警报器名词，后接 sounded 表示发出警报声。','The first sense is a loud device with a rising and falling warning sound.','第一义是发出高低起伏警报声的装置。'),C('siren.s2','factory','At the factory, the siren marked the end of the night shift and the start of the morning shift.','工厂的汽笛标志着夜班结束、早班开始。','siren marked the end','工业汽笛可用来提示换班，不一定是危险警报。','The second sense is a loud whistle used by a ship or factory for a signal.','第二义是轮船或工厂用来发信号的汽笛。'),C('siren.s3','mythology','In the old myth, sailors followed the Siren’s beautiful song toward dangerous rocks.','古老神话中，水手跟随塞壬美妙的歌声驶向危险礁石。','the Siren’s beautiful song','专名 Siren 指神话生物；引申可指诱人却危险的人。','The mythological sense names the alluring creature whose song endangered sailors.','神话义是以歌声诱惑水手的塞壬。')],M('The flood siren gave a warning by remaining silent and producing no sound at all.','The flood siren gave a warning by sounding its rising, falling alarm.','警报器以声音示警，完全无声无法完成此功能。','meaning'),[Q(1,'Why did the flood siren sound?','to warn residents of danger','to announce the end of a factory shift','to lure sailors in a myth','The first sense is a warning device.'),Q(2,'What did the factory siren signal?','the change between shifts','a flood evacuation','a mythical song','The second sense covers industrial signals.'),Q(3,'Who lured sailors with song in the myth?','a Siren','a silversmith','a singleton','The mythological creature is the source of the name.'),Q(1,'What kind of noise does an emergency siren make?','a loud rising-and-falling warning sound','a quiet spoken sentence','no sound at all','The alarm sense uses a loud, changing pitch.')]);
P('sister','Sister is Old English sweostor, from Proto-Germanic *swestr- and a very old Indo-European kinship word; it also names a nun, senior nurse, or related institution.',[C('sister.s1','family','My sister and I share the same parents, but we chose very different careers.','我和姐姐（妹妹）父母相同，但选择了完全不同的职业。','share the same parents','名词指有共同父母的女性手足。','The first sense is a girl or woman with the same parents as another person.','第一义是有相同父母的姐妹。'),C('sister.s2','hospital','The senior sister checked the ward list before the nurses began their rounds.','护士长在护士们开始查房前核对了病房名单。','senior sister','英式医院语境中 Sister 可作资深护士的职称。','The second sense can be a woman in a religious order or a senior nurse title.','第二义可指修女，或英式医院的资深护士。'),C('sister.s3','institutions','The city’s sister museum in Seoul lent two paintings for the new exhibition.','这座城市在首尔的姐妹博物馆为新展览借出了两幅画。','sister museum','sister 用作定语表示关系密切的同类机构。','The third sense is a closely linked organization of the same kind.','第三义指关系密切的同类机构。')],M('The museum called an unrelated airport its sister museum even though it is not a museum or linked institution.','The museum called its closely linked partner museum in Seoul a sister museum.','sister museum 要求同类且有密切关系；无关机场不符合。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why are the two women sisters?','they have the same parents','they work in the same building','one is a museum','The family sense is defined by shared parents.'),Q(2,'Who is the senior sister in this hospital context?','a senior nurse','the nurse’s biological sibling only','a linked museum','Sister can be a title for a senior nurse in some hospitals.'),Q(3,'What is a sister museum?','a closely linked museum of the same kind','any unrelated building','a woman with the same parents','The institutional sense describes a related organization.'),Q(1,'Which phrase uses sister in the family sense?','my younger sister','the sister hospital in another city','Sister Mary at the clinic','The first phrase refers to a female sibling.')]);
P('sit','Sit is Old English sittan, from Proto-Germanic *sitjaną; it can mean take a seated position, place someone seated, take an exam (especially British), or meet officially.',[C('sit.s1','posture','Please sit on the bench while the technician checks your ankle.','请坐在长椅上，让技师检查一下您的脚踝。','sit on the bench','sit 不及物用法表示坐下或保持坐姿。','The first sense is rest with weight on the bottom and upper body upright.','第一义是坐下或保持坐姿。'),C('sit.s2','placing','She sat the toddler on the wide step while she opened the gate.','她打开门时，把幼儿安置在宽台阶上坐好。','sat the toddler on','及物用法带宾语，表示使某人处于坐姿。','The second sense means put someone into a sitting position.','第二义是让某人坐下。'),C('sit.s3','British education','In Britain, he will sit the chemistry exam in June and receive results in August.','在英国，他将于六月参加化学考试，八月得知成绩。','sit the chemistry exam','英式英语中 sit + exam 表示参加考试。','The third sense means take an examination, especially in British English.','第三义是参加考试，常见于英式英语。'),C('sit.s4','government','The council will sit next Monday to hear objections to the new rail line.','委员会下周一将开会听取对新铁路线路的异议。','council will sit','sit 可表示机构正式开会处理公务。','The fourth sense is meet for official business.','第四义是开会或履行公务。')],M('He will sit the exam by refusing to take it and staying home on the test day.','He will sit the exam by attending and taking it in June.','sit an exam 是参加考试，不是拒绝应考。','usage'),[Q(1,'Where should the patient wait?','seated on the bench','standing on the roof','inside the exam paper','Sit in this sense is to take a seated position.'),Q(2,'What did she do with the toddler?','placed the child into a sitting position','asked the child to sit the chemistry exam','held a council meeting','The transitive sense means cause someone to sit.'),Q(3,'What does “sit the exam” mean in British English?','take the examination','write the exam paper for others','sit down after the exam only','The phrase means be an exam candidate.'),Q(4,'Why will the council sit?','to meet officially and hear objections','to take a chemistry exam','to rest on a bench','The institutional sense means hold a formal session.')]);
P('site','Site comes from Latin situs, “position or place,” through French site; it can name a location, an internet group of pages, or the act of placing something.',[C('site.s1','construction','The engineers tested the soil at the site of the proposed footbridge.','工程师在拟建人行桥的选址处检测了土壤。','site of the proposed footbridge','site 指某事将要发生或建造的地点。','The first sense is a place where something is or will be built or done.','第一义是某物所在或将要建造、发生的地点。'),C('site.s2','internet','The museum posted the conservation report on its public site for visitors to read.','博物馆把保护修复报告发布在公众网站上，供访客阅读。','on its public site','site 作 website 的简称，表示互联网网页集合。','The second sense is a group of pages on the internet.','第二义是网站。'),C('site.s3','planning','The planners sited the new clinic beside the bus terminal so patients could reach it easily.','规划人员把新诊所选址在公交总站旁，方便患者前往。','sited the new clinic','site 作及物动词表示把建筑物放在选定位置。','The verb means place or build something in a chosen position.','动词义是把某物建在选定位置。')],M('The planners sited the clinic by choosing its website address rather than selecting any physical location.','The planners sited the clinic beside the bus terminal.','site 作动词是为建筑选址，不是挑选网址。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'Where did the engineers test the soil?','at the proposed bridge location','on the museum website','inside a chemistry exam','Site can name a physical place where something will be built.'),Q(2,'Where did the museum post the report?','on its internet pages','at the bridge foundation','on a bus terminal signpost','Site is also a short form of website.'),Q(3,'What did the planners do?','placed the clinic at a chosen location','uploaded the clinic to a web page','measured the size of a silver bowl','The verb site means locate or place a building.'),Q(1,'Which is a construction site?','the plot where workers will build a bridge','a webpage displaying reports','the act of sitting an exam','The noun sense is the place of a building project.')]);
P('site-specific','Site-specific combines site + specific; it describes art or work made for one particular location rather than for general use.',C('site-specific.s1','art','The site-specific sculpture uses the courtyard’s old brick arches and would lose its meaning if moved.','这件特定场地艺术作品利用了庭院的古砖拱门，移走后便会失去意义。','site-specific sculpture','compound adjective 置于名词前，限定作品是为该地专门创作。','The adjective describes something made for a stated location, not for general use.','该形容词指为某个具体地点而做，不是通用作品。'),M('The sculpture is site-specific because the artist designed it to fit any room and any location equally.','The sculpture is site-specific because it was designed around this courtyard’s arches.','适用于任何地点是通用设计，和 site-specific 的特定地点要求相反。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why would moving the sculpture change its meaning?','it was designed around that courtyard’s features','it is a standard sculpture sold for any room','it is a website page','Site-specific work depends on its particular location.'),Q(1,'Which project is site-specific?','a sound installation built for one train station’s echo','a standard poster printed for any wall','a website template for all users','The work is created for a particular site.'),Q(1,'What does specific contribute in the compound?','particular rather than general','made of silver','quiet and without sound','Specific narrows the work to a stated location.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses site-specific correctly?','The mural responds to this building’s history and layout.','The mural is identical everywhere and made for no location.','The mural is a chemical element.','The phrase describes design tied to a site.')]);
P('sitter','Sitter is sit + -er, naming someone who sits for an artist or photographer, or someone who cares for children or pets while owners are away.',[C('sitter.s1','childcare','We hired a sitter to stay with the twins at home while both parents attended the evening meeting.','父母都去参加晚间会议时，我们请了一位照看者在家照顾双胞胎。','hired a sitter','名词指临时代人照看孩子或宠物的人。','The first sense is a person who cares for children or pets while owners are away.','第一义是主人外出时照看孩子或宠物的人。'),C('sitter.s2','portrait','The portrait’s sitter held still for an hour while the painter studied her profile.','画中的模特静坐了一小时，让画家观察她的侧面。','portrait’s sitter','所有格短语指为艺术家静坐摆姿势的对象。','The second sense is a person who sits for an artist or photographer.','第二义是为画家或摄影师静坐的人。')],M('The portrait sitter posed for the painter by running around the studio and never sitting still.','The portrait sitter posed for the painter by sitting still while the portrait was made.','肖像画中的 sitter 要静坐摆姿势，不是四处奔跑。','context'),[Q(1,'Why was the sitter hired?','to care for the twins while their parents were away','to paint the twins’ portrait','to repair the meeting room','A childcare sitter looks after children temporarily.'),Q(2,'What did the portrait sitter do?','sat still so the painter could study her','watched pets at the parents’ home','carried a road sign','The second sense is the person being painted or photographed.'),Q(1,'Which worker is a sitter in sense 1?','someone caring for a child during an evening out','an artist holding a brush','a person posing in a portrait','The first sense is temporary childcare or pet care.'),Q(2,'In a portrait studio, the sitter is…','the person posing for the artist','the painter’s chair','the person who frames the picture','The noun identifies the model being painted.')]);
P('sitting','Sitting comes from sit + -ing; as a noun it can be one meeting/session or a meal service, and as an adjective it describes someone currently holding office.',[C('sitting.s1','court','The court’s morning sitting ended after the judge heard the final witness.','法官听完最后一名证人后，法院上午的庭审结束了。','morning sitting','名词指一次会议、辩论或法庭审理。','The first noun sense is one occasion of a meeting, debate, or court case.','第一名词义是会议、辩论或庭审的一次。'),C('sitting.s2','dining','The restaurant offers two sittings for dinner so the kitchen can serve guests in groups.','餐馆安排两场晚餐用餐时段，让厨房分批接待客人。','two sittings for dinner','餐饮名词表示一段供应一餐的时段。','The second noun sense is one period when a group is served a meal.','第二名词义是餐馆供应一餐的一场时段。'),C('sitting.s3','politics','The sitting mayor announced that she would seek another term in office.','现任市长宣布将寻求连任。','sitting mayor','现在分词形容词置于职务名词前，表示当前在任。','The adjective means holding an official position at the present time.','形容词义是现任的、在位的。')],M('The sitting mayor is no longer in office and left the position two years ago.','The former mayor left office two years ago; the sitting mayor currently holds the job.','sitting mayor 指现任者，离任两年的人应称 former mayor。','word-choice'),[Q(1,'What ended after the last witness?','one court session','the restaurant’s second meal service','the mayor’s term only','A court sitting is one occasion of a hearing.'),Q(2,'Why are there two dinner sittings?','the restaurant serves guests in two meal periods','the court hears two witnesses','the mayor holds two offices','A sitting can be one period of meal service.'),Q(3,'Who is the sitting mayor?','the person currently holding the office','the former mayor from two years ago','a portrait model','Sitting as an adjective means in office now.'),Q(1,'Which use is a noun for a meeting?','The committee’s sitting lasted two hours.','The sitting mayor spoke.','She is sitting on a chair.','The first noun sense is a session of official work.')]);
P('sitting room','Sitting room is a compound phrase, literally a room for sitting; it is a British term for a household room where people relax together.',C('sitting room.s1','home','Guests gathered in the sitting room after dinner to talk beside the small bookcase.','晚饭后，客人们聚在起居室的小书柜旁聊天。','gathered in the sitting room','复合名词指家人或客人坐着聊天、阅读或看电视的房间。','A sitting room is a home room for sitting, talking, reading, or watching television.','sitting room 是供人坐着聊天、阅读或看电视的家居房间。'),M('The family called the room a sitting room, although everyone stood there to cook and wash dishes.','The family used the sitting room to sit, talk, and read together.','烹饪洗碗的功能对应 kitchen，不是起居室。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Where did the guests talk after dinner?','in the room used for relaxing together','in the kitchen sink','in the courtroom','A sitting room is a domestic living space.'),Q(1,'Which activity suits a sitting room?','reading together on a sofa','washing dishes at the sink','taking an exam','The room is for family or guests to sit and spend time.'),Q(1,'What kind of phrase is sitting room?','a compound noun for a home room','a verb meaning to hold court','a measurement of room size','The phrase names a domestic room.'),Q(1,'Which is closest to sitting room?','a household living room','a courtroom session','a bus terminal','It is a room where people sit, talk, or relax.')]);
P('situate','Situate comes from Latin situare, “place or locate,” from situs “position”; it can locate a building or place an idea within its wider context.',[C('situate.s1','location','The lodge is situated above the lake, where the eastern trail meets the old road.','旅舍位于湖面上方，处在东侧步道与旧路的交会处。','is situated above','常用被动形式 be situated 表示建筑的地理位置。','The first sense means put a building or town in a particular place.','第一义是把建筑或城镇置于某地点。'),C('situate.s2','scholarship','The historian situates the letter in the political crisis that followed the election.','历史学家把这封信放在选举后发生的政治危机背景中考察。','situates the letter in','situate A in a context 表示联系背景解释对象。','The second sense describes something in relation to its wider context.','第二义是联系更广背景来描述某事物。')],M('The historian situated the letter in its context by refusing to discuss the events surrounding it.','The historian situated the letter in its context by explaining the political events surrounding it.','把对象置于背景中需要说明相关背景，而不是完全拒绝讨论。','context'),[Q(1,'Where is the lodge situated?','above the lake near the trail junction','inside the historian’s letter','at the end of the exam','The first sense gives a building’s location.'),Q(2,'What did the historian do with the letter?','explained it against the political events of its time','moved the physical lodge','made the letter easier to read only','The academic sense relates an item to its wider context.'),Q(1,'Which sentence uses situate as location?','The clinic is situated beside the station.','The historian situates the poem in its era.','The meeting will sit next week.','The first sentence locates a building.'),Q(2,'To situate an argument in context is to…','relate it to the wider circumstances','put it in a kitchen sink','make it a single word','The second sense is contextual placement.')]);
P('situated','Situated is the past participle of situate, used adjectivally for a location or a person/organization’s circumstances or position.',[C('situated.s1','geography','The clinic is situated beside the station, within walking distance of the river market.','诊所位于车站旁，步行即可到达河边集市。','is situated beside','be situated + place 表示物理坐落位置。','The first sense means located in a particular place or position.','第一义是位于特定地点或位置。'),C('situated.s2','circumstances','With two experienced translators on staff, the agency is well situated to handle the treaty talks.','有两位经验丰富的译员在职，这家机构很有条件处理条约谈判。','well situated to handle','well situated to + verb 表示条件有利、处境适合。','The second sense is being in a particular condition or well placed to act.','第二义指处于某种境地，或具备有利条件。')],M('The agency is well situated to translate the talks because it has no translators and cannot access the documents.','The agency is well situated to translate the talks because it has experienced translators and the documents.','没有人员和材料不构成有利条件，不能称 well situated。','context'),[Q(1,'Where is the clinic located?','beside the station','inside the treaty text','at a dinner sitting','Situated in this sense gives a physical location.'),Q(2,'Why is the agency well situated for the talks?','it has experienced translators and access to documents','it has no translators','it is physically next to a lake only','The circumstances sense means well placed to do something.'),Q(1,'Which phrase describes geographic location?','The school is situated on the hill.','The company is situated to compete because of its skills.','The court had one sitting.','The first use locates the school physically.'),Q(2,'“Well situated to help” means…','in a favorable position or condition to help','sitting in a particular chair','located exactly at the river’s mouth','The second sense is favorable circumstances.')]);
P('situation','Situation entered English through French situation from Latin situs, “position”; it names circumstances, a place’s position, or (in older usage) a job.',[C('situation.s1','events','The situation improved when both sides agreed to reopen the crossing before winter.','双方同意在冬季前重新开放通道后，局势有所好转。','situation improved','抽象名词概括某一时刻存在的条件和事件。','The first sense is the set of conditions and events at a particular time.','第一义是某一时刻的各种条件和事件。'),C('situation.s2','geography','The house has a fine situation above the harbour, with clear views in both directions.','这所房子的位置很好，坐落在港口上方，可以清楚眺望两侧。','fine situation above','较正式的 situation 可指建筑物在周围环境中的位置。','The second sense is the place of a building or town among its surroundings.','第二义是建筑或城镇相对于周围环境的位置。'),C('situation.s3','employment','The old notice offered a situation as a clerk to anyone with accurate handwriting.','旧招聘启事为字迹工整的人提供了一份文书工作。','offered a situation as','旧式招聘用语 a situation as 指一份职位或工作。','The third sense is an old-fashioned word for a job.','第三义是旧式说法，指一份工作。')],M('The old notice offered a situation as a clerk, but the sentence says no job was available.','The old notice offered a situation as a clerk to a qualified applicant.','offer a situation 表示提供工作，与“没有职位”矛盾。','meaning'),[Q(1,'What changed in the border situation?','the crossing would reopen before winter','the house moved above the harbour','a clerk changed handwriting','Situation here means current conditions and events.'),Q(2,'Why was the house said to have a fine situation?','its position above the harbour gave broad views','it had an easy job opening','the border crossing was closed','The formal geographical sense concerns location among surroundings.'),Q(3,'What did the old notice offer?','a job as a clerk','a house with a harbour view','a set of changing circumstances','The older sense of situation is a job or position.'),Q(1,'Which paraphrase fits “the situation is improving”?','the conditions and events are getting better','a building has moved to another place','a clerk has accepted a job','The common sense refers to circumstances at a time.')]);
P('situational','Situational is situation + -al, an adjective meaning caused by or connected with circumstances at a particular moment rather than a fixed trait.',C('situational.s1','psychology','Her calm was situational: she stayed relaxed in familiar rooms but panicked in crowded stations.','她的平静是由情境决定的：在熟悉房间里很放松，在拥挤车站却会恐慌。','calm was situational','冒号后解释该状态随所处环境改变。','Situational describes a state connected with circumstances of a moment.','situational 指由某一时刻的情境造成或关联的状态。'),M('His fear was situational, meaning he felt exactly the same in every environment and circumstance.','His fear was situational, appearing only in the crowded station.','situational 与特定情形相关，不表示各环境都固定相同。','distinction'),[Q(1,'Why was her calm situational?','it changed with the setting','it was a permanent personality trait','it described the size of a room','Situational means connected with circumstances.'),Q(1,'Which is a situational response?','a person panics only in a crowded lift','a person has the same trait in every setting','a building is located beside a river','The response is tied to a particular circumstance.'),Q(1,'What does -al contribute in situational?','an adjective meaning related to a situation','a plural ending','a person who sits for a portrait','The suffix turns situation into an adjective.'),Q(1,'Which paraphrase fits situational calm?','calm caused by the conditions at that moment','calm that never changes in any setting','a room designed for sitting','The word contrasts circumstances with a fixed trait.')]);
P('six','Six is Old English siex, from Proto-Germanic *sehs and an ancient Indo-European number root; it names the whole number and can stand for six o’clock or the sixth day when clear.',[C('six.s1','counting','The laboratory set out six glass vials, one for each water sample.','实验室摆出了六只玻璃瓶，每份水样对应一只。','six glass vials','数词限定可数复数名词，表示五和七之间的整数。','The first sense is the whole number between five and seven.','第一义是五和七之间的整数。'),C('six.s2','time','The evening train leaves at six, so we should reach the platform by 5:40.','晚班火车六点发车，因此我们应在五点四十分前到站台。','at six','在时间语境中 six 可简略表示六点钟。','The second sense can stand for six o’clock or a date when context supplies it.','第二义在语境清楚时可表示六点或六号。')],M('The train leaves at six, and the timetable says this means 6:30.','The train leaves at six, which the timetable defines as 6:00.','在这里 six 表示六点整，不是六点半。','measurement'),[Q(1,'How many vials were set out?','six','five','seven','Six is the integer between five and seven.'),Q(2,'When does the train leave?','at 6:00','at 5:40','at 6:30','At six means six o’clock in this context.'),Q(1,'Which set contains six objects?','six water samples','five samples and one empty space','seven vials','The number sense counts exactly six.'),Q(2,'What does “meet me at six” usually mean?','meet at six o’clock when the time context is clear','meet with six people every time','meet on the sixth floor only','The word can abbreviate a clock time.')]);
P('sixteen','Sixteen is the compound number six + ten, from Old English sixtene; it is the cardinal number after fifteen and before seventeen.',C('sixteen.s1','age','The sixteen-year-old volunteer completed the first-aid course before joining the event team.','这名十六岁的志愿者在加入活动团队前完成了急救课程。','sixteen-year-old volunteer','复合数词作形容词，连字符连接年龄定语。','Sixteen is the number ten plus six.','sixteen 是十加六所得的数。'),M('The volunteer was sixteen years old, which means she had reached age sixty.','The volunteer was sixteen years old, between fifteen and seventeen.','十六和六十是不同数值，不能互换。','measurement'),[Q(1,'How old was the volunteer?','sixteen','six','sixty','Sixteen is ten plus six.'),Q(1,'Which number comes after fifteen?','sixteen','fourteen','sixty','Sixteen follows fifteen in the counting sequence.'),Q(1,'What does sixteen-year-old modify?','volunteer','course','event team','The compound number describes the volunteer’s age.'),Q(1,'Which equation equals sixteen?','10 + 6','6 × 10','60 − 6','Sixteen is six added to ten.')]);
P('sixteenth','Sixteenth is six + -teenth, forming the ordinal number 16; as a fraction, one sixteenth is one of sixteen equal parts.',[C('sixteenth.s1','ordinal','Their office is on the sixteenth floor, two levels above the fourteenth.','他们的办公室在第十六层，比第十四层高两层。','sixteenth floor','序数词修饰 floor，标明序列中的第 16 位。','The first sense is number 16 in a series.','第一义是序列中的第十六。'),C('sixteenth.s2','fraction','The recipe uses only a sixteenth of a teaspoon of the strong spice.','这份食谱只用十六分之一茶匙的浓烈香料。','a sixteenth of a teaspoon','a sixteenth 表示把整体分为十六等份后的其中一份。','The fractional sense is one of sixteen equal parts.','分数义是十六等份中的一份。')],M('The office is on the sixteenth floor, which is the position immediately before the fifteenth.','The office is on the sixteenth floor, after the fifteenth and before the seventeenth.','序数顺序中第十六在第十五之后、第十七之前。','measurement'),[Q(1,'Where is the office?','on floor 16','on floor 14','on floor 60','Sixteenth is the ordinal for position 16.'),Q(2,'How much spice does the recipe use?','one of sixteen equal parts of a teaspoon','sixteen full teaspoons','one sixth of a teaspoon','A sixteenth is 1/16 of the whole.'),Q(1,'What is the ordinal form for position 16?','sixteenth','sixteen','sixty','The -teenth form is ordinal.'),Q(2,'A sixteenth of a quantity is…','one part when the whole is divided into sixteen equal parts','sixteen times the whole','one part out of six','The fractional sense represents 1/16.')]);
P('sixth','Sixth is the ordinal form of six, from Old English siexta; it can mean position number six or one of six equal parts.',[C('sixth.s1','sequence','June is the sixth month of the year, following May and preceding July.','六月是一年中的第六个月，排在五月之后、七月之前。','sixth month','序数词表示在固定序列中的第六位。','The first sense is number six in an ordered series.','第一义是序列中的第六。'),C('sixth.s2','fraction','The siblings divided the cake evenly, so each received a sixth.','兄弟姐妹把蛋糕平均分开，因此每人分到六分之一。','received a sixth','a sixth 作分数名词，表示六等份中的一份。','The second sense is one of six equal parts.','第二义是六等份中的一份。')],M('June is the sixth month because it comes after July and before August.','June is the sixth month because it comes after May and before July.','June 的位置在五月之后、七月之前，不在七月之后。','measurement'),[Q(1,'Which month is sixth?','June','May','July','June occupies position six in the calendar year.'),Q(2,'How much cake did each sibling receive?','one of six equal shares','six whole cakes','one of sixteen equal shares','A sixth is 1/6 of a whole.'),Q(1,'What does sixth indicate in “sixth month”?','ordinal position six','a count of sixteen','the color silver','The first sense is the sixth item in sequence.'),Q(2,'If a whole is split equally among six people, one share is…','a sixth','a sixteenth','sixty','The fraction is one of six equal parts.')]);
P('sixtieth','Sixtieth is sixty + -th, forming an ordinal for position 60; it also names one of sixty equal parts.',[C('sixtieth.s1','anniversary','The library will mark its sixtieth anniversary with a public exhibition of its first catalogues.','图书馆将通过公开展出首批目录来纪念其六十周年。','sixtieth anniversary','序数词表示第六十个周年纪念。','The first sense is number 60 in a series.','第一义是序列中的第六十。'),C('sixtieth.s2','measurement','The instrument can detect an error of one sixtieth of a degree.','这台仪器能检测到六十分之一度的误差。','one sixtieth of a degree','分数名词表示把一度分成六十等份后的其中一份。','The second sense is one of sixty equal parts.','第二义是六十等份中的一份。')],M('The library’s sixtieth anniversary celebrates 16 years since it opened.','The library’s sixtieth anniversary celebrates 60 years since it opened.','sixtieth 是第六十周年，不是第十六周年。','measurement'),[Q(1,'How many years does the anniversary mark?','sixty','sixteen','six','Sixtieth is the ordinal for 60.'),Q(2,'What is one sixtieth of a degree?','one of sixty equal parts of a degree','one of six degrees','sixty degrees','The fraction is 1/60 of one degree.'),Q(1,'Which anniversary is the sixtieth?','the 60th','the 16th','the 6th','The ordinal number is sixty.'),Q(2,'Which expression is a sixtieth?','1/60','1/6','60/1','A sixtieth is one part of sixty equal parts.')]);
P('sixty','Sixty is Old English sixtig, from Proto-Germanic *sekhs-tig, literally a group of six tens; it is six times ten.',C('sixty.s1','number','The warehouse counted sixty crates, arranged in six rows of ten.','仓库清点了六十个箱子，分成六排、每排十个。','sixty crates','数词表示六乘十的总数。','Sixty is the number equal to six times ten.','sixty 是六乘十所得的数。'),M('The warehouse counted sixty crates in six rows of ten, which totals only sixteen crates.','The warehouse counted sixty crates in six rows of ten.','六排每排十个共六十个，不是十六个。','measurement'),[Q(1,'How many crates were counted?','sixty','sixteen','six','Sixty equals six times ten.'),Q(1,'What is 6 × 10?','sixty','sixteen','sixtieth','The cardinal number is sixty.'),Q(1,'How are the crates arranged?','six rows of ten','ten rows of six hundred','sixty rows of one hundred','Six tens make sixty.'),Q(1,'Which number is six tens?','sixty','sixth','sixteen','Sixty is the product of six and ten.')]);
P('sizable','Sizable is size + -able, meaning large enough to be noticed or important; sizable is the usual American spelling, while sizeable is common in British English.',C('sizable.s1','scale','The grant was sizable enough to fund two years of fieldwork across the island.','这笔拨款相当可观，足以资助在岛上开展两年的实地调查。','sizable enough to fund','sizable 描写金额大到值得注意或能产生实际作用。','Sizable means large enough to be worth noticing.','sizable 表示大到值得注意。'),M('The grant was sizable enough to fund two years of work, although it amounted to only one cent.','The grant was sizable enough to fund two years of work because it was substantial.','一分钱不足以资助两年调查，与 sizable enough 的语境矛盾。','measurement'),[Q(1,'What could the grant pay for?','two years of fieldwork','one cup of tea only','a sixteenth of a window sill','Sizable indicates an amount large enough to matter.'),Q(1,'Which amount might be called sizable?','a substantial grant funding a major project','one cent in a two-year budget','a single drop of water','The adjective means large enough to be noticeable.'),Q(1,'Which spelling is an accepted American form?','sizable','sizzable','sizible','Sizable is the standard American spelling.'),Q(1,'What does -able add to size here?','the sense of being of a noticeable size','the meaning “without size”','a past-tense meaning','The adjective means having considerable size.')]);
P('size','Size came through Middle English from Old French sise, a fixed measure or quantity; it names dimensions or a standard clothing measure and can mean estimate or make to measure.',[C('size.s1','dimensions','What is the size of the storage room, including its ceiling height?','储藏室的尺寸是多少，包括层高？','size of the storage room','size 指长宽高等大小或规模。','The first sense is how large or small a person or thing is.','第一义是人或事物的大小、规模。'),C('size.s2','clothing','The shop had the jacket in my size, so I tried it on before ordering.','店里有我尺码的夹克，因此我下单前先试穿了。','in my size','服装语境中 size 是标准衣服或鞋的号数。','The second sense is a standard measurement used for clothes or shoes.','第二义是服装或鞋的标准尺码。'),C('size.s3','assessment','Before making an offer, the negotiator sized up the risks of each route.','提出报价前，谈判代表估量了每条路线的风险。','sized up the risks','size up 是动词短语，表示判断人、问题或情况的分量。','The verb means judge how large a problem or person is; size can also mean make to a measurement.','动词义可表示估量问题，也可指按尺寸制作。')],M('The shop said the jacket was my size, but its label showed a standard measurement far too small for me.','The shop said the jacket was my size because its measurement matched my usual fit.','尺码必须与穿着者合适；过小的标准尺寸不能称为合身尺码。','measurement'),[Q(1,'What does the question “What is the size of the room?” ask about?','how large the room is','what the room costs','who sits in the room','Size in the first sense concerns dimensions.'),Q(2,'Why did the shopper try on the jacket?','the shop had the standard clothing measurement that fit','the jacket was a room measurement','the negotiator had sized up a route','The clothing sense is a standard garment measurement.'),Q(3,'What did the negotiator do?','assessed the risks of each route','measured the jacket label','sat down in a room','Size up means evaluate or estimate.'),Q(2,'Which phrase refers to a shoe measurement?','What size do you wear?','How large is the room?','She sized up the problem.','The second sense is a standard clothing or shoe size.')]);
})();
